hadiths[605]{hadithnumber,text}:
"12101","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when they performed li'an: As for you two, you have known that I do not know the unseen."
"12102","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali, he said: When the matter of the two who performed li'an happened before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I do not love to be the first of the four."
"12103","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have had no contact with my wife since the dusting of the palms. Its dusting is that they were pollinated, then left dusty forty days, not watered after pollination. He said: He found a man with his wife. The husband was yellowish, thin-shanked, straight-haired, and the one she was accused with was bulky toward blackness, curly-haired, swollen. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make clear. Then he performed li'an between them. She brought a child resembling the one she was accused with. Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, the like of this hadith, and al-Qasim added: Ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had said to Ibn Abbas: Is she the woman to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned without proof I would have stoned her? Ibn Abbas said: No, but that woman had announced in Islam."
"12104","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, he said: Abu al-Zinad informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed li'an between al-Ajlani and his wife, and she was pregnant. Her husband said: I have not approached her since the dusting of the palms, and the dusting of the palms is that they were not watered after pollination for two months. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make clear. He said: They claim the woman's husband was thin of forearms and shanks, reddish-haired, and the one she was accused with was black. She brought a black boy, curly-haired, thick of forearms, fleshy of shanks. Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said: Ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had said to Ibn Abbas: Is she the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned without proof I would have stoned her? Ibn Abbas said: No, that woman had announced in Islam."
"12105","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr say: We were in Kufah differing about li'an, some saying: We do not separate them. Sa'id said: I met Ibn Umar and asked him about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the two sons of al-Ajlan, and said: By Allah, one of you is a liar, is there a repenter among you? Neither confessed, so they performed li'an, then he separated them."
"12106","Ayyub said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: O Messenger of Allah, my dower? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If you were truthful, it is hers for what you made lawful of her; if you lied, that makes it more due to her, or as he said."
"12107","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the two who performed li'an: Your reckoning is upon Allah; one of you is a liar; you have no way to her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my wealth? He said: You have no wealth; if you were truthful it is for what you made lawful of her private part; if you lied it is farther from you than her."
"12108","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: How is li'an? He said: He testifies four testimonies by Allah, a testimony, then let him testify four that he is among the truthful; then he says: Upon him is the curse of Allah if he is among the liars. She is the like of that, and she says: Upon her is the wrath of Allah if he is among the truthful."
"12109","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Abu al-Sha'tha, that he said: The torment is averted from her, that he performs li'an, as it is averted from her."
"12110","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: A commander among the commanders informed me that I perform li'an between a man and his wife, so I performed li'an between them. He said: I said: How did you do? He said: As it is in the Book of Allah Almighty."
"12111","From al-Thawri, he said: He says: I testify by Allah that I am among the truthful in what I charged her with of adultery. He begins, then she after."
"12112","From al-Thawri, from Bayan, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Li'an is greater than stoning."
"12113","From al-Thawri, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab say: The curse and wrath fall upon the more lying of them."
"12114","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: One who slanders her, he said: He is given the hadd."
"12115","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, they said: Whoever accuses the woman after li'an is flogged the hadd."
"12116","From Abdillah ibn Kathir, from Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah and al-Sha'bi, that they said: About one who performs li'an with his wife then says to her after separation: The child is not mine? They said: He is flogged. And I asked al-Hakam and Hammad, and they said the like, from Hushaym ibn Bashir, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, the like of Shu'bah's hadith."
"12117","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, they said: Whoever accuses the son of li'an is flogged the hadd."
"12118","From Hushaym, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, they said: Whoever accuses the son of li'an is flogged."
"12119","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about one who marries his foster sister unknowingly until he consummates with her, then accuses her, then knows that, he said: There is no li'an between them; they are separated; he is flogged; the child is attached to him."
"12120","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who married a woman, and when she died he was told she is his foster sister, he said: He is fined the dower and does not inherit her. And Qatadah said: He inherits her."
"12121","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: If a man says to the son of li'an: O son of so-and-so, for the one he was disowned from, he is disciplined and not flogged."
"12122","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If a man says: O son of so-and-so, to the man for the one he was disowned from, he said: He should not be called after him, and he did not mention a hadd upon him."
"12123","From al-Thawri, he said: Whoever says to the son of li'an: O son of so-and-so whom he was disowned from, there is no hadd upon him."
"12124","From al-Thawri about li'an: If the one who performed li'an with his mother claims him after he dies, it is not allowed, because he only claimed wealth; if he claims while alive, he is beaten and he is attached to him."
"12125","From al-Thawri, he said: If a man accuses his wife while sick, he performs li'an with her, then dies of that sickness, she inherits him while in the waiting period, because it came from him; if she dies he does not inherit her."
"12126","From al-Thawri, he said: The claim of women about a child that she bore him is not allowed except with proof."
"12127","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abdillah, meaning Ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: I wrote to a man of Banu Zurayq of Madinah's people, asking about the son of li'an, who inherits him? He wrote to me that he asked, and they agreed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed him to the mother, and made her in the position of his father and mother."
"12128","From al-Thawri, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, he said: Abdillah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to me, he said: I wrote to a brother of mine of Banu Zurayq: For whom did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decree the son of li'an? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed him to his mother; she is in the position of his father and mother. Sufyan said: His mother inherits all the wealth."
"12129","From al-Thawri, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The son of li'an is called after his mother; whoever accuses his mother saying: O son of the adulteress, is beaten the hadd; his mother is his kin, he inherits her and she inherits him. Sufyan said: All the wealth."
"12130","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Mas'ud said: All the inheritance of the son of li'an is his mother's."
"12131","From al-Thawri, from al-Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: The son of li'an's kin is his mother; they inherit him and pay blood-money for him; his mother's accuser is beaten; his father and mother do not come together."
"12132","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali, he said: The kin of the son of li'an is his mother's kin."
"12133","From a companion of his, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali and Ibn Mas'ud, they said: The kin of the son of li'an is his mother's kin."
"12134","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Who inherits the son of li'an who leaves his mother alone? He said: Hers is a third, and his mother's kin get the rest. I said: And he leaves his daughter? He said: Hers is half, and his mother's kin get the rest."
"12135","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, he said: The sunnah ran in the son of li'an that he inherits her, and his mother inherits from him what Allah ordained for her."
"12136","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: His mother inherits a third from him, and the rest is in the treasury. And Ibn Abbas said it too."
"12137","From Ma'mar, he said: Al-Nakha'i and al-Sha'bi differed about the inheritance of the son of li'an, so they sent a messenger to Madinah asking about that. He returned and told them from Madinah's people that the woman who performed li'an with her husband in the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated them, she married and bore children, then her son over whom she performed li'an died. His mother inherited a sixth from him, his brothers inherited a third from him, and the rest was between his brothers and mother by their inheritances; his mother got a third, his brothers two thirds. From Isma'il ibn Abdillah, from Ibn Awn, the like of Ma'mar's hadith."
"12138","From Ma'mar, he said: It reached me that some say: His mother gets a third, and his mother's kin get the rest. He said: And I see, if there are brothers with her, they get the rest; if he has no mother, Ibn Tawus said: I was told from a man of Madinah's people that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The maternal uncle is heir of one with no heir, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is patron of one with no patron. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Tawus, the like."
"12139","From Ma'mar, he said: I heard some of Madinah's people say: His mother gets a third; if she is of the Arabs, two thirds are in the treasury; if he is of the Arabs, two thirds are in the treasury; if she is of the clients, his mother's clients get a third."
"12140","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: The child of adultery, his mother bore him free, he said: His inheritance is the inheritance of li'an."
"12141","From al-Thawri, he said: The inheritance of the child of adultery is the inheritance of the son of li'an."
"12142","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about children of adultery: One who claims them does not inherit them, and they inherit from the mothers' side, because we do not know, perhaps they are not one, and we do not believe their mothers if they say that; if she bears two boys from adultery and one dies, the other inherits a sixth."
"12143","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: If a man leaves his daughter, his maternal brothers, and his maternal uncles, all the wealth is his daughter's."
"12144","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: About a man who accuses his Jewish or Christian wife, he said: Upon her is the wrath of Allah; she is his wife as she is; he does not perform li'an with her."
"12145","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa informed me, from Makhul, he said: There is no li'an between them."
"12146","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Hammad, they said: If a Muslim accuses a pregnant Christian wife, there is no li'an between them."
"12147","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ayyash informed me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Of the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instruction to Attab ibn Asid: that there is no li'an between four and their husbands: the Jewess, the Christian woman with the Muslim, the slave woman with the freeman, and the freewoman with the slave."
"12148","Ma'mar said, and Ata al-Khurasani narrated it to me, that he heard what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Attab ibn Asid: If a man says to women: One of you has committed adultery, not knowing which, and did not say: She is so-and-so, there is no hadd and no li'an."
"12149","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, he said: He does not perform li'an with the Jewess or Christian woman; he only performs li'an with one whom, if he accused her, he would be beaten."
"12150","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: If a freeman accuses his slave wife, the child is attached to him, there is no li'an between them, no hadd upon him, they are not separated; she remains his wife as she is."
"12151","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Ata and Mujahid, they said: There is no li'an between the Muslim and the Jewess, the Christian woman, and the owned woman."
"12152","From al-Thawri, from one who heard Ibrahim say: He does not perform li'an with the Jewess, the Christian woman, or the owned woman. Her division and the freewoman's division are equal, their waiting period and divorce, meaning the Jewess and Christian woman; there is no li'an between them, no inheritance; the Christian woman is married over the free Muslim woman, but the slave woman is not married over the Christian woman."
"12153","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from Tawus, Mujahid, al-Sha'bi, from al-Hakam, and from Ibrahim, they said: About the Jewess and Christian woman under the Muslim whom he accuses: he performs li'an with her. So was their saying about the freeman under whom is a slave woman. They said: There is no hadd upon their accuser."
"12154","From Ma'mar, from a man, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr, he said: There is no li'an between the Jewess, the Christian woman, the owned woman, and the Muslim."
"12155","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: If a Muslim accuses his Christian wife, he performs li'an with her."
"12156","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: He performs li'an in every couple."
"12157","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Her accuser is flogged; Allah Almighty named her among the chaste."
"12158","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb said, from Abdillah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: Four, there is no li'an between them and their husbands: the Jewess, the Christian woman under the Muslim, the freewoman with the slave, the slave woman with the freeman, the slave woman with the slave, and the Christian woman with the Christian."
"12159","From Ma'mar, from Hammad, he said: If a man accuses the Christian woman with the Muslim, there is no hadd upon him."
"12160","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: If he accuses the Christian woman under the Muslim, he is flogged the hadd."
"12161","From Musa, from al-Zuhri, he said: If she has a Muslim child, her accuser is flogged for the sanctity of Islam; else no hadd upon her accuser."
"12162","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, about a man who accused a Christian woman with a Muslim child, Umar flogged him some thirty-odd lashes."
"12163","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Whoever accuses a Christian man or woman is disciplined, not given the hadd."
"12164","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa informed me, he said: Our saying for one upon one who slanders a woman of the Scripture people, even if a Muslim slave."
"12165","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Raja ibn Haywah informed me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, he said: Sulayman stood with us while we were people of Sham in his caliphate, with him Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. Umar said: What do you say about a man who says to a man: O drinker of wine? He said: We said: We give him the hadd. Umar said: Glory be to Allah, we give the hadd only to one who accuses a Muslim."
"12166","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Nafi', freedman of Ibn Umar, say: There is no hadd upon any Muslim who slanders any polytheist, Christian, Jew, or Magian."
"12167","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata said: Slandered a Muslim man whose father is of the polytheists, punishment and no dispute."
"12168","From al-Thawri, from Tariq and Mutarrif ibn Tarif, they said: We were with al-Sha'bi when a Muslim man and a Christian came to him, one accusing the other. The Christian was beaten eighty for the Muslim, and he said to the Christian: What is in you is greater than accusation, so he left. That was raised to Abd al-Hamid, who wrote about it to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz mentioning what al-Sha'bi did, and Umar approved it."
"12169","From al-Thawri, about a Christian who accused a Christian woman: They are not beaten for each other when they litigate to Islam's people, as the Muslim is not beaten for them when he accuses them; likewise they are not beaten for each other."
"12170","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: If a man denies the pregnancy of his concubine, physiognomists are called for him; if he had secluded her, it is his; what he said against her is not allowed."
"12171","From Abdillah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, that Umar said: Whoever among you has intercourse with his slave girl, let him seclude her; none of you admits intercourse with his slave girl but I attach the child to him."
"12172","Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from Umar, that he said: It reached me that men among you practice withdrawal; when the slave girl becomes pregnant, he says: It is not mine. By Allah, no man among you who does that is brought to me but I attach the child to him. Whoever wishes, let him practice withdrawal; whoever wishes, let him not."
"12173","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim informed me, that Umar passed a slave girl drawing upon camels, watering, and said: Perhaps this one's master has intercourse with her then denies her child; yet if he denied, I would bind him to him."
"12174","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It was narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Salim ibn Abdillah, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, that he said: O people, hold onto your slave girls; none has intercourse with a slave girl and she bears but I attach her child to him. From Ibn Jurayj, from Musa, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, from Umar, the like."
"12175","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar informed me, that in a letter of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, that Umar decreed about a man's slave girl who came to him and mentioned to him that he used to have her while she was a servant differing for his needs, that she became pregnant, so he doubted her pregnancy and confessed intercourse with her. Umar said: O people, what is with men who have their slave girls, then one says when she becomes pregnant: It is not mine? Any man who confesses intercourse with his slave girl and she becomes pregnant, her child is his, whether he secluded her or not; if she bears, she is confined to him, not sold, inherited, or gifted; he enjoys her while alive; when he dies she is free, not counted in her child's share, no debt reaches her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that a child may not own his parent, nor is he left in his ownership."
"12176","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu Nawfal Muslim ibn Amr informed me, that he heard Abdillah ibn Umayr ibn al-Harith narrate, that Abu Bakr, or Umar, had a black slave girl, practiced withdrawal with her, then sold her. Her master went with her until on the road he desired her and she refused him; there was a shepherd, so he called him and spoke her language, and he told her he is her master. She said: I became pregnant from my former master, and in my religion no man touches me in pregnancy from another. Her master wrote to Abu Bakr or Umar and told him the news, and he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waited until next day, their sitting place being the Stone. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, upon him peace, came to me in this sitting from Allah Almighty: that none of you has choice over Allah when the seeker seeks, but: He grants to whom He wills females and grants to whom He wills males. Acknowledge your child. So he wrote that about her."
"12177","From Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ghaylan ibn Anas, he said: Abu Bakr bought a non-Arab slave girl from a man who had had her and she became pregnant by him. Abu Bakr wanted to have her, so she resisted him and told him she was pregnant. He raised that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: She guarded, so Allah guarded for her; none of you, when he seeks by that seeking, has choice over Allah. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned her to her owner."
"12178","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: It was said to Ata: The umm walad of Maysarah, freedman of Ibn Bazan, claims her son is not Maysarah's. He said: She is not believed; the child is for the bed, and for the adulterer the stone. He said: Ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr asked him about Maysarah's affair, and said: Will you not leave physiognomy for him? He said: No; the child is for the bed, and for the adulterer the stone. He said: And I say: If a freewoman says of her child by the man, she is belied and beaten."
"12179","From al-Thawri, he said: If a man has intercourse with his slave girl, coming in and going out, then she becomes pregnant and he says: It is not mine, it is not attached to him."
"12180","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Dhakwan, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit used to have a slave girl of his, pleasing her because she was his slave girl. When she bore him, he disowned her child and beat her a hundred, then freed the boy. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Abu al-Zinad, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, the like, except he said: The slave girl was Persian."
"12181","From al-Thawri: one may not disown the child of the slave-woman if he had acknowledged him, but if he disavowed him before acknowledging him, he is not attributed to him."
"12182","From Muhammad ibn Umar, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Ibn Abbas had relations with a slave-girl of his, and he used to practice withdrawal with her, then she gave birth, and he disowned her child."
"12183","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ziyad, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas while he was insulting the boy and his mother with his tongue; he said: he is indeed your son, so he called him and mounted his mother on a riding animal; he said: and Ibn Abbas had disowned him."
"12184","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from a man of the people of Madinah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to practice withdrawal with a slave-girl of his, then she became pregnant and that grieved him, and he said: O Allah, do not attach to the family of Umar one who is not of them; he said: then she gave birth to a black boy, so he asked her, and she said: from the camel-herd; he said: then he rejoiced."
"12185","From al-Thawri concerning the mother of the child who said: my child is not from my master; he said: she is not believed, the master has more right to the child, and there is no beating upon her if he acknowledges him."
"12186","Ibn Jurayj reported: I said to Ata: a man absent from his wife, and she had not sought his permission to go out, may she go out for circumambulation or visiting a sick relative; he said: no, he refused sternly; I said: her father is dying; but he refused to permit her regarding her father; he said: and I say she may visit him and a near relative; Ibn Umar once left Friday prayer and went to a relative who had invited him."
"12187","From al-Thawri, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from his uncle Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: no one may enter upon a woman whose husband is absent except a mahram; lo, even if it is said: her in-laws, lo, her in-laws are death."
"12188","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: while he is absent, none may enter upon her except a mahram."
"12189","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: no man may enter upon a woman whose husband is absent; he said: then a man stood and said: a brother of mine or a cousin of mine is out fighting and entrusted his family to me, may I enter upon them; he said: then he struck him with the stick, then said: come near, come, stay at the door and do not enter, and say: do you need anything, do you want anything."
"12190","From Mamar, from al-Hasan, that Amr ibn al-As sought permission to see Ali but did not find him, so he returned, then sought permission again and found him, and he spoke to the wife of Ali about his need; Ali said: as if your need was with the woman; he said: yes, indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade entering upon women whose husbands are absent; Ali said to him: yes, indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade entering upon women whose husbands are absent."
"12191","From Mamar, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Arfajah, he said: Abu Musa said to the mother of his son Abu Burdah: when a man who is not a mahram enters upon you, call someone of your family to stay with you, for when a man and a woman are alone, Satan runs between them."
"12192","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: it is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah to be alone with a woman who is not a mahram except with a mahram present."
"12193","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he said: even a mahram of hers may not enter unless there is with her a man of her family who is a mahram of hers; he said: I almost am certain that he traced it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12194","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: a man used to enter upon her in his presence, may he enter after him; he said: no, and when he is present, a non-mahram may enter upon her unless he refuses; I said: may he sit on his bed; he said: yes, that is only forbidden lest he make his bed a place of adultery."
"12195","From Ibn Uyaynah, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: the likeness of one who visits a woman whose husband is absent to sit on her bed and talk with her is like one bitten by black snakes."
"12196","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah, he said: a man came from a journey, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: did you stay with so-and-so woman and close her door upon you; no man may be alone with a woman."
"12197","Sulayman al-Ahwal reported that he heard Amr ibn Dinar asking Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman about withdrawal with women; he said: Abu Said al-Khudri claimed that a man of the Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have a slave-girl who carries water for me, and I practice withdrawal with her, only fearing a child, and the Jews claim it is the minor burying alive; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: the Jews lie, the Jews lie; he said: then we asked Abu Salamah: did you hear it from Abu Said; he said: no, but a man informed me of it from him."
"12198","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: some Muslims came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have slave-girls and we practice withdrawal with them, and the Jews claim it is the minor burying alive; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: the Jews lie, the Jews lie, indeed they lie; if Allah wills to create him, none can repel him."
"12199","From al-Thawri, from Mansur and al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have a slave-girl and I practice withdrawal with her; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: whatever soul Allah has decreed to come forth, it will come; from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir, the like, except he said: a man of the Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12200","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me, while sitting with Ata, that a man sitting with Ibn Abbas asked him about withdrawal with women; he said: there is no harm in it; then Ibn Abbas called a slave-girl of his who shoots arrows and said: I do it with this one; Ata then said: a man of the people said to him: some people say it is the minor burying alive; Ibn Abbas said: glory be to Allah, it is a drop, then a clot, then a lump, then bones, then the bones are clothed; he said: and he spoke with his hand, joining his fingers and stretching them to the sky, and said: withdrawal happens before all of this."
"12201","From Mamar and al-Thawri, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: I had a slave-girl with whom I practiced withdrawal, then she bore me the dearest of people to me."
"12202","From Malik, from Damrah ibn Said, from al-Hajjaj ibn Amr, that he was sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit when Ibn Fahd, a man of Yemen, came to him and said: O Abu Said, I have slave-girls, not my wives whom I conceal, more pleasing to me than them, and not all of them please me to bear children from me, may I practice withdrawal; Zayd said: give him a ruling, O Hajjaj; he said: I said: may Allah forgive you, we sit with you to learn from you; he said: give him a ruling; he said: I said: she is your tilth, if you wish you water it, and if you wish you leave it thirsty; he said: and I used to hear that from Zayd; then Zayd said: he spoke the truth."
"12203","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Mujahid, that Ibn Abbas used to practice withdrawal with a slave-girl of his, then show it to her fearing she might bring something."
"12204","From al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: a concubine of Ali named Jumanah or Umm Jumanah informed me, she said: Ali used to practice withdrawal with her, and we said to him about it, and he said: shall I keep alive what Allah has caused to die."
"12205","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ali, from his grandmother, that she was a concubine of al-Hasan ibn Ali, and he used to practice withdrawal with her."
"12206","From Hushaym, from Musab ibn Sad, that Sad used to practice withdrawal with the mother of his child."
"12207","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he was asked about withdrawal with slave-girls, and he said: it was done."
"12208","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ata, that he disliked withdrawal with a free woman except with her permission, saying: it is part of her right."
"12209","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: the free woman is consulted about withdrawal, and the slave-girl is not consulted."
"12210","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Humayd al-Araj, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: no withdrawal with a free woman except with her permission."
"12211","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from a man, from Ikrimah, he said: there is no harm if a man practices withdrawal with his wife when he seeks her permission and she permits him."
"12212","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, Zayd ibn Thabit, and Ibn Abbas used to practice withdrawal."
"12213","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata narrated to me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, when withdrawal was mentioned to him, saying: we used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"12214","From al-Thawri, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from al-Nakhai, that Ibn Masud saw no harm in withdrawal."
"12215","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud was asked about withdrawal, and he said: if Allah took the covenant of a soul from the loins of Adam, then poured it upon a rock, He would bring it forth from that rock; so practice withdrawal, and if you wish, do not."
"12216","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, he said: they used to say: the drop in which Allah has decreed a child, even if placed upon a rock, a child would come forth from it."
"12217","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Mujahid, he said: we asked Ibn Abbas about withdrawal, and he said: I will delay you from asking; they said: so we asked in our house and returned to him, and he recited to us: We created man from an essence of clay, until: then We produced him as another creation; then he said: how can it be burying alive until it passes through this creation."
"12218","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that a man said to Ibn Abbas: some people think it is the minor burying alive, meaning withdrawal; he said: glory be to Allah, it is a drop, then a clot, then a lump, then bones, then the bones are clothed with flesh; he spoke with his hand, joining his fingers then stretching them to the sky, and said: withdrawal is before all of this, how can it be burying alive; then the spirit is breathed into him, and withdrawal is before all of this."
"12219","From al-Thawri, from Salamah ibn Tammam, from al-Shabi, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about withdrawal, and he said: no son of Adam can kill a soul whose creation Allah has decreed; she is your tilth, if you wish you water it, and if you wish you leave it thirsty."
"12220","From Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aflah, from a mother of the child of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that Abu Ayyub used to practice withdrawal."
"12221","And Ibn Jurayj mentioned it, from Ziyad, from Abu al-Zinad, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, that Abu Ayyub used to practice withdrawal."
"12222","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Said, he said: I heard Ibn al-Musayyib saying: the Companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, differed about it; by Allah, it is only your tilth, if you wish you water it, and if you wish you leave it thirsty."
"12223","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about withdrawal, and he said: do you indeed do it; they said: yes; he said: there is no harm if you do not do it, for Allah has not decreed a soul to create it except it will be."
"12224","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, that Ibn Umar used to dislike withdrawal; Mamar said: and I know al-Zuhri only said: and Umar used to dislike that."
"12225","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ubaydullah ibn Humayd al-Araj informed me, from Urwah, from Iyad, he said: by Allah, I was standing in prayer when I heard Abdullah ibn Umar speaking strictly about withdrawal, so I turned to him and said: is this your own opinion; he said: yes."
"12226","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Abd al-Ala, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: Ali was asked about withdrawal with women, and he said: that is the hidden burying alive."
"12227","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Ibn Masud, he said concerning withdrawal: it is the hidden burying alive."
"12228","From Hushaym, from Abu Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas took my beard when it grew and said: O Said, have you married; I said: no, and it is not in my mind today; he said: if there is a trust in your loins, it will come forth."
"12229","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, he said: Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that he entered upon Said ibn Jubayr when he was young and his face had grown, he said: he said to me: have you married, O Khallad; he said: I said: no, and it is not in my mind today; he said: then he struck my back with his hand, then said: if there is a trust in your back, it will come forth."
"12230","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ziyad informed me, from Abu al-Zinad, from Kharijah ibn Zayd: that Abu Ayyub used to practice withdrawal."
"12231","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu Qazah informed me and Ata, from a man of Banu Qushayr, from his father, that he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: what is the right of my wife upon me; he said: feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not forsake, and do not forsake except in the house."
"12232","From al-Thawri concerning a woman complaining that her husband does not come to her; he said: he has three days, and she has a day and a night."
"12233","From al-Thawri, from Jabir and Malik ibn Mighwal, from al-Shabi, he said: a woman came to Umar and said: my husband is the best of people, he stands the night and fasts the day; Umar said: you have praised your husband well; Kab ibn Sur said: she has complained in veiled speech; Umar said: speak out what you said; he said: I see you should treat him as a man with four wives, he has three days and their nights, and she has a day and a night."
"12234","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from al-Shabi, he said: a woman came to Umar and said: O Commander of the Faithful, my husband is the best of people, he fasts the day and stands the night, by Allah I dislike complaining about him while he acts in obedience to Allah, mighty and majestic, and peace and mercy of Allah be upon you; Kab ibn Sur said: I never saw a complaint more severe nor an accusation more veiled; he said: what do you say; he said: she claims she has no share of her husband; he said: if you understood that, judge between them; he said: O Commander of the Faithful, Allah has permitted of women two, three, and four, so she has of every four days a day in which he breaks fast and stays with her, and of every four nights a night in which he sleeps with her."
"12235","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: a woman came to Umar and said: my husband stands the night and fasts the day; he said: do you order me to forbid him standing the night and fasting the day; then she left, then returned to him after that and said the like to him, and he answered her with the like of his first saying; Kab ibn Sur said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, she has a right; he said: what is her right; he said: Allah has permitted him four, so make one of the four for her, she has in every four nights a night, and in four days a day; he said: then Umar called her husband and ordered him to spend with her of every four nights a night, and to break fast of every four days a day."
"12236","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ibn Abi Labid informed me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that a woman came to Umar and said: my husband is a truthful man, he stands the night and fasts the day, and I cannot bear that; he said: then he called him and said: she has of every four days a day, and in every four nights a night."
"12237","From Zamah and others, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: it reached me that a woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: her husband does not approach her, so he sent for her husband and asked him, and he said: I have grown old and my strength is gone; Umar said: do you approach her once every month; he said: more than that; Umar said: in how long; he said: I approach her once in every purity; Umar said: go, for in this is what suffices a woman."
"12238","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, he said: Khawlah bint Hakim, wife of Uthman ibn Mazun, entered upon Aishah looking disheveled, and she asked her: what is wrong with you; she said: my husband stands the night and fasts the day; then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Aishah and she mentioned that to him, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met Uthman and said: O Uthman, monasticism has not been prescribed for us, do you have no example in me, for by Allah I am the most fearful of Allah among you and the most careful of His limits."
"12239","Al-Zuhri said, and Said ibn al-Musayyib informed me that he heard Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, indeed refused celibacy for Uthman, and had he permitted it for him, we would have been castrated."
"12240","From Mamar, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: whoever practises celibacy is not of us."
"12241","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: one whom I trust informed me that Umar, while circumambulating, heard a woman saying: this night has grown long and its side is wet, and sleeplessness keeps me, with no beloved to play with; were it not for fear of Allah, nothing like it, the sides of this bed would shake; Umar said: what is wrong with you; she said: you sent my husband away four months ago, and I long for him; he said: did you intend evil; she said: Allah forbid; he said: control yourself, for it is only the post to him, so he sent for him, then entered upon Hafsah and said: I ask you about a matter that concerns me, so relieve me of it, how long does a woman long for her husband; she lowered her head in shyness; he said: indeed Allah is not shy of the truth; so she indicated three months, otherwise four; then Umar wrote: armies shall not be detained beyond four months."
"12242","From Mamar, he said: it reached me that Umar ibn al-Khattab heard a woman saying: this night has grown long and its side is dark, and sleeplessness keeps me, with no beloved to play with; were it not for the One above the heavens, whose is the Throne, the sides of this bed would shake; in the morning Umar sent for her and said: are you the one who said such and such; she said: yes; he said: why; she said: you dispatched my husband in these expeditions; he said: then Umar asked Hafsah: how long can a woman endure from her husband; she said: six months; so after that Umar used to rotate his expeditions every six months."
"12243","From al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, he said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man saying to his wife: O my sister, and he rebuked him; and he passed by a man saying: by trust, and he said: you said: by trust, you said: by trust."
"12244","Al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah reported: Amr ibn Shuayb informed me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a woman divorced by her husband wanted to take her child from her, and she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, when my belly was a vessel for him, my breast a drink for him, and my lap a shelter for him, his father wants to take him from me; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: you have more right to him as long as you do not marry."
"12245","Ibn Jurayj reported: Amr ibn Shuayb said, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that a woman came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a son of hers, and said: O Messenger of Allah, when my belly was a vessel for him, my breast a drink, and my lap a shelter, his father wants to take him from me; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: you have more right to him as long as you do not marry."
"12246","From Mamar, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating that Abu Bakr judged against Umar concerning his son that he is with his mother, and said: his mother has more right to him as long as she does not marry."
"12247","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: a woman has more right to her child as long as she does not marry, and when she marries, his father takes him."
"12248","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from Ikrimah, he said: a woman disputed with Umar before Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both, and he had divorced her, and he said: she is more affectionate, gentler, more merciful, kinder, and more compassionate, and she has more right to her child as long as she does not marry."
"12249","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata al-Khurasani informed me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab divorced his Ansari wife, mother of his son Asim, then met her carrying him at Mahsar, and met him weaned and walking, and he took his hand to take him from her, and contended with her until he hurt the boy and he cried, and said: I have more right to my son than you; they disputed to Abu Bakr, and he judged for her, and said: her scent, her warmth, and her bed are better for him than you, until he grows and chooses for himself; and Mahsar is a market between Quba and Hudaybiyah, and the people of Madinah told me: he only met his grandmother al-Shamus carrying him at Mahsar."
"12250","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: Umar saw Asim his son with his grandmother, his mothers mother, as if he pulled him from her, and when Abu Bakr saw him coming, Abu Bakr said: she has more right to him; he said: then he did not argue with him."
"12251","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Taym narrated to me that this wife of Umar was the daughter of Asim ibn al-Aqlah, and al-Aqlah is of Banu Amr ibn Awf of the Aws."
"12252","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr saying: a man of Iraq divorced his wife while pregnant, and he did not divorce her concerning the pregnancy, nor the birth, nor suckling, nor after that, nor his son, until people once set out for Hajj, and a man of the company, the father being in the party, said: O so-and-so, do you see your son in the party, would you know him if you saw him; he said: no, by Allah; he said: this is your son, so he pulled his bridle and went off, and when they came to Umar, his mother clung with her cloak, then chanted: leave to you, O Ubayd al-Rahman: pregnancy is a year and weaning two years; Umar heard her speech and said: leave her, then she told him the story, and he gave the youth a choice, and he chose his mother, and she went off with him."
"12253","From Ibn Jurayj, that he heard Abdullah ibn Abdullah saying: a father and mother disputed over a son of theirs before Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he gave him a choice, and he chose his mother, and she went off with him."
"12254","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ismail ibn Ubaydullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, he said: a boy was disputed before Umar, and he said: he is with his mother until his tongue expresses, then he chooses."
"12255","From Mamar, he said: one who heard Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, saying: Umar judged in his caliphate that he is with his mother until he grows and chooses."
"12256","From al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu al-Walid, he said: an uncle and a mother disputed before Umar, and Umar said: your mothers pull is better for you than your uncles plenty."
"12257","From al-Thawri, from Yunus ibn Ubaydullah al-Jarmi, from Umarah ibn Rabiah al-Jarmi, he said: I disputed with my uncle over my mother, from the people of Basrah, before Ali; he said: my uncle and my mother came, and they sent me to Ali, so I called him and he came, and they told him, and he said: your mother or your uncle, which is dearer to you; he said: I said: my mother, three times; he said: and they used to prefer three in everything; then he said to me: you are with your mother, and this brother of yours, when he reaches what you reached, will choose as you chose; he said: and I was a boy."
"12258","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, that he judged that the child is with his mother when the house is one, and there is in their maintenance what suffices them; he said: they looked, and there were small sheep and camels, and he said: there is no surplus in this beyond these."
"12259","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ziyad, from Hilal ibn Usamah, from Sulaym Abu Maymunah, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: a mother and father came disputing to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, over a son of theirs, and she said to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: may my father and mother be ransom for you, my husband wants to take my son, and he has given me drink from the well of Abu Inabah and benefited me; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O boy, this is your father and this is your mother, take the hand of whichever you wish; so he took his mothers hand, and she went off with him."
"12260","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ziyad informed me, from Hilal ibn Usamah, that Abu Maymunah Sulaym, a freedman of Madinah, a truthful man, said: while I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah, a Persian woman came with a son of hers who had sufficed her, and her husband had divorced her, and she said: O Abu Hurayrah, then she spoke in Persian, my husband wants to take my son; Abu Hurayrah said: cast lots for him, and he spoke to her in that; then her husband came to Abu Hurayrah and said: who disputes me over my child; Abu Hurayrah said: O Allah, I do not say this, I heard a woman come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while I sat with him, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, my husband wants to take my son, and he has given me drink from the well of Abu Inabah and benefited me; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: cast lots for him; her husband said: who disputes me over him, O Messenger of Allah; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: cast lots for him, O boy, this is your father and this is your mother, take the hand of whichever you wish; so he took his mothers hand, and she went off with him."
"12261","Ibn Jurayj reported: al-Ajlah informed me, he said: I am the first of Allah's creation in Kufah to spread this report, that a grandmother and a mother disputed before Shurayh, and the grandmother said in verse: O Abu Umayyah, we came to you, and you are the man we come to, your son and his mother came to you, and both of us ransom him, a boy whose father perished, hoping you will raise him, had you remained unmarried I would not dispute you over him, you married, so give him, and pride should not take you, O judge, this is my story in him; and the mother said in verse: O judge, the grandmother has told you a tale, so hear from me and do not hasten my reply, I console myself over my son, and my liver carried his liver, when he was in my lap an orphan, lost, alone, I married a man of good who guarantees me support, who gives him love and suffices me his loss; Shurayh said: leave to the evening; then they returned to him, and he said: the judge has heard what you said and judged between you, then decided with a manifest judgment between you, and upon the judge is effort if he is just; he said to the grandmother: show the boy, your son is your core despite ailments, had she been content she would have had before her claim a substitute."
"12262","Ibn Jurayj reported: I heard Ata asked about the child of the contract-slave and the slave from a free woman; he said: his mother has more right to him because she is free."
"12263","From al-Thawri concerning the child of the slave and the contract-slave; he said: his mother has more right to him because she is free."
"12264","Al-Thawri reported, from Uthman al-Butti, from Abd al-Hamid al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather, that his grandfather embraced Islam and his wife refused to embrace Islam, and he came with a small son of his who had not reached puberty; he said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seated the father here and the mother here, then gave him a choice, and said: O Allah, guide him, and he went to his father."
"12265","From Mamar, from Amr, from al-Hasan, he said: when an apostate apostatizes from Islam, what is between him and his wife is cut; al-Thawri said: and the man and woman are alike."
"12266","From al-Thawri, he said: when a woman apostatizes and she has a husband who has not consummated with her, she has no dowry, and what is between them is cut; but if he had consummated with her, she has the full dowry."
"12267","From Mamar, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said concerning a man captured who becomes Christian: when that is known, his wife is cleared of him and waits three menstrual cycles."
"12268","From al-Thawri, from Musa ibn Abi Kathir, he said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyib about the apostate, how long does his wife wait; he said: three menstrual cycles; he said: I said: he is killed; he said: then four months and ten days."
"12269","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi embraced Islam with ten wives, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to take four of them; he mentioned it from Salim, from Ibn Umar; Mamar said: and one who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying: he chooses four of them; he said: and Qatadah said: he keeps the first four."
"12270","From Ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, he said: he keeps the first four; and al-Thawri said it, from Ibrahim."
"12271","From al-Thawri, from a man, from Ibrahim, concerning a man with two sisters under him who then embrace Islam; he said: he leaves the latter and keeps the former, and may not approach her until the waiting period of the latter ends, and if he married them in one contract, he leaves them both."
"12272","From Mamar, from al-Kalbi, from a man, from Qays ibn al-Harith al-Asadi, he said: I embraced Islam with eight wives under me, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: choose four of them."
"12273","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, said: Islam separated between four and the sons of their husbands: Humaynah bint Abi Talhah was with Khalaf ibn Sad, then al-Aswad ibn Khalaf succeeded him; and Fakhitah bint al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib was with Umayyah ibn Khalaf, then Safwan ibn Umayyah succeeded him; and Umm Ubayd bint Damrah was with al-Aslat, then Abu Qays ibn al-Aslat of the Ansar succeeded him; and Mulaykah bint Kharijah was with Zabban ibn Sinan, then Manzur ibn Zabban succeeded him; and Islam came while al-Qays ibn al-Harith al-Asadi had eight wives, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: divorce and keep four, and divorce four; then one would say: I adjure you by Allah and companionship, and another: I adjure you by Allah and kinship."
"12274","Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, said: Islam came while Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf had six wives: Atikah bint al-Walid, Aminah bint Abi Sufyan, Barzah bint Masud al-Thaqafi, the daughter of Amir ibn Malik, Fakhitah bint al-Aswad, and Umm Wahb bint Abi Umayyah; so he divorced Umm Wahb, who was old, and left the one who had been with his father in ignorance, Fakhitah bint al-Aswad; Atikah bint al-Walid was among the last he married, and the daughter of Amir ibn Malik was among those he kept, until he divorced Atikah in the rule of Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"12275","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, said: Islam came while Urwah ibn Masud had ten wives, Sufyan ibn Abdullah al-Thaqafi had nine wives, and Abu Sufyan ibn Harb had six wives; Amr said: they are six of Jumah."
"12276","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Abu Wahb al-Jayshani, from Abu Khirash, from al-Daylami, that he embraced Islam with two sisters under him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to choose whichever he wished and divorce the other."
"12277","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who embraces Islam with wives under him; he said: he keeps the first four and leaves the rest."
"12278","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man who embraces Islam with two sisters under him; he said: he keeps the first of them; Mamar said: and one who heard al-Hasan informed me, saying: he chooses whichever he wishes."
"12279","From Mamar, from Awf, he said: Amr ibn Hind narrated to me that a man embraced Islam with two sisters under him, and Ali ibn Abi Talib said to him: you shall leave one of them, or I shall strike your neck."
"12280","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Shuayb informed me that whatever inheritance in ignorance belonged to its heir, after their manner therein, and whatever marriage or divorce in ignorance Islam found, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, confirmed it, except usury; whatever usury Islam found not yet taken, it is returned to the seller as capital, and the usury dropped; and it is mentioned that people spoke to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about their inheritances, for they inherited elder from elder to return it, but he refused."
"12281","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata: has it reached you that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, confirmed people in what Islam found them upon, of divorce, marriage, or inheritance; he said: nothing reached us but that."
"12282","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: when inheritances fall, whoever embraces Islam over an inheritance, it is nothing."
"12283","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: every wealth divided in ignorance is upon the division of ignorance, and every wealth Islam finds is upon the division of Islam."
"12284","From Mamar, from Qatadah and Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: whoever embraces Islam over an inheritance before it is divided inherits from it."
"12285","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: whatever marriage in polytheism, unless one embraces Islam upon it, he remains upon it."
"12286","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, confirmed what inheritance in ignorance there was, and what Islam found undivided is divided upon the division of Islam."
"12287","From Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, he said: Nafi narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged that whatever inheritance was divided in ignorance is upon its division in ignorance, and what Islam finds is upon the division of Islam."
"12288","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Islam came while women were with men, and I know them only to have remained with them in Islam upon the marriage of ignorance."
"12289","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, that Zaynab daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, embraced Islam while her husband Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi was a polytheist, then he embraced Islam after a while, and no new marriage was made; and Mamar mentioned it, from Khalid, from al-Shabi."
"12290","From al-Thawri, he said: when two Christians embrace Islam, they remain upon their marriage."
"12291","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning one who embraces Islam over an undivided inheritance; he said: he has no right, for inheritances fell before he embraced Islam, and slaves are of that standing."
"12292","Ibn Jurayj reported: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali informed him that Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi informed him, and he had married the daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, by Khadijah; he said: he was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in bonds, and Zaynab freed him; Amr said: I think they only remained upon their marriage of ignorance."
"12293","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Zaynab daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, embraced Islam while her husband al-As ibn al-Rabi remained a polytheist, then he embraced Islam after that, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept them upon their marriage."
"12294","From Israil ibn Yunus, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: a woman embraced Islam in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then her first husband came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I embraced Islam with her and my Islam with her was known; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took her from her other husband and returned her to her first husband."
"12295","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that it reached him that women in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, embraced Islam in their lands without emigrating, while their husbands when they embraced Islam were disbelievers, among them Atikah daughter of al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, under Safwan ibn Umayyah, who embraced Islam on the day of the conquest at Makkah, while her husband Safwan fled from Islam and boarded the sea; then he sent to him his cousin Wahb ibn Umayr with a cloak of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as safety for Safwan; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called him to Islam and to come to him, if he wished to embrace Islam he would, otherwise the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would grant him two months; when Safwan came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with his cloak, he called on horseback before the people: O Muhammad, this Wahb brought your cloak claiming you called me to come, if a matter from me pleases you you accept it, otherwise you grant me two months; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: dismount, O Abu Wahb; he said: no, by Allah, I shall not dismount until you clarify to me; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: no, rather you have four months; he said: then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out toward Hawazin with an army, and sent to Safwan borrowing tools and weapons he had; Safwan said: willingly or by force; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: no, rather willingly; so Safwan lent him the tools and weapons he had, and Safwan marched as a disbeliever with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and witnessed Hunayn and Taif as a disbeliever while his wife was Muslim, yet the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not separate him from his wife until Safwan embraced Islam, and his wife remained with him by that marriage; then Umm Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham embraced Islam on the day of the conquest at Makkah, while her husband Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl fled from Islam until he reached Yemen, so Umm Hakim bint al-Harith journeyed until she reached Yemen and called him to Islam, and he embraced Islam, and she brought him to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw him, he leapt to him joyfully with no cloak upon him until he pledged him; then it has not reached us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, separated them, and she remained with him upon that marriage; but it has not reached us that a woman emigrated to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while her husband remained a disbeliever in the abode of disbelief, except her emigration separated her from her disbelieving husband, unless he comes emigrating before her waiting period ends, for it has not reached us that a woman was separated from her husband when he came to her emigrating while she was in her waiting period."
"12296","From Ayyub, from Mamar, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, that Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl fled on the day of the conquest, then his wife wrote to him and brought him back, and he embraced Islam, and she had embraced Islam before that, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept them upon their marriage."
"12297","From Humayd, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: Zaynab daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, embraced Islam a year before her husband Abu al-As, then he embraced Islam, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned her with a new marriage."
"12298","From Ibn Jurayj, from a man, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Zaynab daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, embraced Islam and emigrated after the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the first emigration, while her husband Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi was a polytheist at Makkah, then Abu al-As fought at Badr as a polytheist and was captured and ransomed, being wealthy, then fought at Uhud also as a polytheist, then returned from Uhud to Makkah, then stayed at Makkah as Allah willed, then went to Syria as a trader, and some Ansar captured him on the Syrian road; Zaynab entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: the Muslims, the least of them grants protection; he said: what is that, O Zaynab; she said: I granted protection to Abu al-As; he said: I have honored your protection, then he did not honor the protection of a woman after her; then he embraced Islam and they remained upon their marriage; Umar proposed to her to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, meanwhile, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned that to her, and she said: Abu al-As, O Messenger of Allah, as you know, and he was an excellent in-law, if you see fit to wait for him; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell silent at that; he said: and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib embraced Islam at Rawha on the return of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the conquest, and came to Jumanah daughter of Abi Talib as a polytheist, and she embraced Islam, and they remained upon their marriage; and Makhramah ibn Nawfal, Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, and Hakim ibn Hizam embraced Islam at Marr al-Zahran, then came to their polytheist wives, who embraced Islam, and they remained upon their marriages; the wife of Makhramah was Shafa daughter of Awf, sister of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, the wife of Hakim was Zaynab bint al-Awwam, and the wife of Abu Sufyan was Hind daughter of Utbah ibn Rabiah; Ibn Shihab said: and with Safwan ibn Umayyah, besides Atikah daughter of al-Walid, was Aminah daughter of Abi Sufyan, who also embraced Islam with Atikah after the conquest, then Safwan embraced Islam after staying with them."
"12299","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab used to say: her husband is given a choice when she embraces Islam before him, if he embraces Islam she is his wife, otherwise Islam separates them; he said: and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote: when she embraces Islam before him, Islam removes her from him, as a slave-girl is removed from a slave when she is freed before him."
"12300","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from al-Hasan and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: when he embraces Islam while she is in her waiting period, he has more right to her; al-Thawri said: and Ibn Shubrumah said it also."
"12301","From al-Thawri concerning covenanted polytheists when one of them embraces Islam: whenever raised to the ruler, he offers him Islam and separates them; he said: and al-Shabi said: every separation is divorce; he said: and our companions said: whatever comes from his side is divorce, and whatever comes from her side is separation, not divorce."
"12302","From al-Thawri, he said: when both are belligerents and one embraces Islam, the marriage is cut."
"12303","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Basri, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: concerning a Christian woman under a Christian man, when the woman embraces Islam; he said: a Christian man shall not be over a Muslim woman, they are separated."
"12304","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, he said: the son of the woman between whom Umar separated when he offered him Islam and he refused, informed me, so he separated them."
"12305","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: the women of the People of the Book are lawful for us, and our women are forbidden to them."
"12306","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: Islam is offered to him, if he embraces Islam she is his wife, otherwise Islam separates them."
"12307","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: what if a woman embraces Islam while her husband is a polytheist, and her waiting period does not end before he embraces Islam; he said: he has more right to her; I said: how, when Islam separated them; he said: I do not know, by Allah."
"12308","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a woman who embraces Islam while her husband is a polytheist, and her waiting period does not end before he embraces Islam; he said: they are kept upon their marriage, unless their matter was raised to the ruler, who separates them; Mamar said: and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said it."
"12309","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, he said: a woman embraced Islam among the people of Hirah while her husband did not embrace Islam, and Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote concerning her: give her a choice, if she wishes she leaves him, and if she wishes she stays with him."
"12310","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, that Ali said: he has more right to her as long as he does not take her out of her town."
"12311","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: he has more right to her as long as he does not take her out of her land of emigration."
"12312","From al-Thawri and Qatadah, they said: it is not lawful for you to marry a Jew, a Christian, a Magian, nor a man of other than your religion."
"12313","From al-Thawri, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote that a Muslim marries a Christian woman, and a Christian does not marry a Muslim woman, and an emigrant marries a bedouin woman, but a bedouin does not marry an emigrant woman, lest he take her out of her land of emigration."
"12314","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: the women of the People of the Book are lawful for us, and our women are forbidden to them."
"12315","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ata, he said: there is no harm in marrying women of the People of the Book, but Muslims do not marry Arab women."
"12316","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning His saying: and do not marry polytheist women; he said: polytheist women among those not of the People of the Book."
"12317","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that Hudhayfah married a Jewish woman in the time of Umar, and Umar said: divorce her, for she is a live coal; he said: is it unlawful; he said: no; he said: why should Hudhayfah divorce her, for his saying, until after that he divorced her."
"12318","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata was asked who of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married among the People of the Book; he said: Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman."
"12319","From al-Thawri, from al-Salt ibn Bahram, from Abu Wail, that Hudhayfah married a Jewish woman, and Umar wrote to him to leave her."
"12320","From al-Thawri, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote that a Muslim marries a Christian woman, and a Christian does not marry a Muslim woman, and an emigrant marries a bedouin woman, but a bedouin does not marry an emigrant woman, lest he take her out of her land of emigration; and whoever gives a gift to a relative, his gift is valid, and whoever gives a gift to a non-relative and is not rewarded for his gift, he has more right to it."
"12321","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amir ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nistas informed me that Talhah ibn Ubaydullah married the daughter of a Jewish chief; he said: Umar insisted upon him but to divorce her."
"12322","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, that Talhah ibn Ubaydullah married a Jewish woman."
"12323","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: a man of my people in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married a woman of the People of the Book."
"12324","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: there is no harm in marrying them."
"12325","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman while at Kufah, having married a woman of the People of the Book, writing: leave her, for you are in the land of the Magians, and I fear the ignorant will say: a disbelieving woman, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married her, and they will ignore the concession from Allah and marry Magian women, so leave her."
"12326","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah being asked about a Muslim marrying a Jewish or Christian woman, and he said: We married them at the time of the conquest at Kufa, along with Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, when we could hardly find many Muslim women; then when we returned, we divorced them. He said: Their women are lawful for us, and our women are unlawful for them."
"12327","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, they both said: It is not lawful for you to marry a Jewish woman, nor a Christian woman, nor a Magian woman."
"12328","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata was asked about a Magian who had combined a woman and her daughter (in marriage), then accepted Islam. He said: It is more beloved to me that he keep away from both of them."
"12329","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: One whom I trust informed me that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to Adi ibn Adi concerning a Magian who had combined a woman and her daughter and then all of them accepted Islam, that he should separate him from both of them."
"12330","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, concerning a Magian who combined a woman and her daughter, then they accepted Islam: he must part from both of them, and he may never marry either one of them."
"12331","From Ma'mar, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Whatever is forbidden within what is lawful is even more strictly (forbidden) within what is unlawful."
"12332","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who combined two Magian sisters, then they accepted Islam, he said: The two sisters are separated in Islam."
"12333","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man divorced his wife during polytheism, making the divorce decisive, whatever it was, then they both accepted Islam. He said: I do not see her as lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"12334","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Men divorced women in the pre-Islamic period, then Islam came, and they did not return to their husbands."
"12335","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, that he used to uphold (the validity of) divorce (pronounced) during polytheism."
"12336","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a Christian woman divorced by her husband while both were Christians, then they accepted Islam afterwards, and she had not married another husband. (The report ends here as transmitted.)"
"12337","From al-Thawri, from Firas al-Hamdani, he said: I asked al-Sha'bi about one who divorced during polytheism, then accepted Islam. He said: Islam only added strength and firmness to it."
"12338","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: Umar was asked about a man who divorced his wife twice in the pre-Islamic period and once in Islam, and Umar said: I neither command you nor forbid you."
"12339","Then Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: As for me, I command you: your divorce during polytheism counts as nothing. Ma'mar said: And Qatada used to give fatwa by it, saying: Your divorce during polytheism counts as nothing."
"12340","From al-Thawri, concerning combining four women of the People of the Book, he said: There is no harm in that."
"12341","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that he used to say: The woman of the People of the Book is like the free Muslim woman; her waiting period, her divorce, and the division (of nights) for her, when she is with a Muslim woman. He said: And she may be married in addition to a Muslim woman, and whoever marries her has become chaste (muhsan); they were named muhsanat (chaste women)."
"12342","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa said to me: The case of the Jewish and Christian woman is like the case of the free Muslim woman: divorce, waiting period, chastity (ihsan), and the division (of nights) between them and the free Muslim woman."
"12343","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that the woman of the People of the Book, her waiting period, her divorce, and her division (of nights) are like that of the Muslim woman. He said: And I heard al-Zuhri saying the same."
"12344","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from a man of Muzayna, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned a Jew who had committed adultery with a Jewess."
"12345","From Ibn Uyayna, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, concerning His saying: And the chaste women of those who were given the Book, he said: When she guards her private part and bathes from major impurity."
"12346","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatada, they both said: A Jewish woman may be married in addition to a Muslim woman."
"12347","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Is there marriage or sale of a woman of the People of the Book to a Magian? He said: I do not like that."
"12348","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Ata, that he disliked a Christian woman being with a Magian, and disliked a Christian woman being sold to a Magian."
"12349","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying, concerning a man who has a Muslim slave woman and a Christian slave marrying the slave to the slave woman? He said: No."
"12350","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a Christian woman under a Christian man, who accepts Islam before he consummates with her? He said: She separates from him, and she has no dowry. From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, the same; he said: And al-Thawri said, and others said: She has half the dowry, because she called him to Islam."
"12351","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: She separates from him, and she has half the dowry. Qatada said: And likewise the slave woman under a slave, who is freed before he consummates with her."
"12352","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muhammad informed me, from a man, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that he said: They are separated, and she has half the dowry, because the divorce now came from his side."
"12353","From Rabah, from Abd al-Karim al-Basri, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, concerning a Christian woman under a Christian man, who accepts Islam before he consummates with her, he said: They are separated, and she has no dowry."
"12354","From al-Thawri, concerning a polytheist who divorced a polytheist woman, and she did not complete her waiting period until she accepted Islam, he said: She observes three menstrual cycles, and she has no inheritance. And he said, concerning a polytheist who died leaving a polytheist wife, and she accepted Islam before her waiting period ended, he said: She observes four months and ten days, counting what had passed of her waiting period during polytheism before she accepted Islam."
"12355","From Ibn Jurayj, he said, I say: If a polytheist divorces a polytheist woman without making it decisive, then she accepts Islam before her waiting period ends, she observes the waiting period of Muslim women, counting what she observed during her polytheism. And if he made it decisive, it is likewise: like a slave woman who is divorced and observes one menstruation, then is freed. And if she does not accept Islam until her waiting period ends, then what she observed suffices her, and her waiting period is whatever it was during her polytheism, and his divorce is whatever it was during their polytheism, upon that basis if they both accept Islam. And if he divorced her decisively while both were polytheists, then he died before her waiting period ended, then she accepted Islam, she observes the menstruation for what passed and does not observe the waiting period of one whose husband died, because of the decisive divorce. And if she accepted Islam after the decisive divorce before he died, then he died, it is likewise. And if he divorced her without making it decisive, then she accepted Islam, then he died before her waiting period ended, and she accepted Islam after his death, she observes the waiting period of one whose husband died, because the Islam was after his death; just as when he divorces her without making it decisive, then she accepts Islam before her waiting period ends, she observes the waiting period of a Muslim woman, counting what passed of her waiting period during her polytheism, for she accepted Islam while she was his wife, then she does not begin the waiting period of a divorced woman anew."
"12356","Ibn Jurayj reported: I said to Ata: What if today a woman of the polytheists comes to the Muslims and accepts Islam, is her husband compensated for her? Due to Allah's saying in al-Mumtahana: Then give those whose wives have gone the like of what they spent. He said: No; that was only between the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the people of the treaty, between him and them."
"12357","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: That was only a truce between the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Quraysh on the day of al-Hudaybiya; it ended on the day of the conquest, and her husband is not compensated for her with anything."
"12358","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: That has ended."
"12359","From al-Thawri, concerning His saying: And give them what they spent, he said: It was between the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the people of Mecca, and it is not acted upon today."
"12360","Ibn Jurayj reported: I said to Ata: Then if a woman now comes from the people of the treaty? He said: Yes, he is compensated. He said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not press those who came of the women of Quraysh; he only stipulated conditions upon them and did not press them."
"12361","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: The Christians of the Arabs are not People of the Book; the People of the Book are only the Children of Israel, to whom the Torah and the Gospel came. As for those of the people who entered among them, they are not of them."
"12362","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abida, that Ali used to dislike the slaughtered animals of Banu Taghlib, saying: They hold to nothing of Christianity except drinking wine. From Hisham, from Abida, the same."
"12363","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from Ibn Sirin, from Abida, from Ali, that he said: Do not eat the slaughtered animals of the Arab Christians, for they hold to nothing of Christianity except drinking wine."
"12364","From Ma'mar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about the slaughtered animals of the Arab Christians. He said: There is no harm in it; whoever professes a religion is of its people, and their women may be married."
"12365","From Ma'mar, from Ata al-Khurasani, he said: There is no harm; have you not heard Allah saying: And among them are unlettered ones who do not know the Book."
"12366","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: And whoever takes them as allies among you, then he is of them."
"12367","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in their slaughtered animals."
"12368","From al-Thawri, from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Allah made their slaughtered animals lawful, and your Lord was never forgetful."
"12369","From al-Thawri, from Abu al-Ala Burd ibn Sinan, from Ubada ibn Nasiy, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, he said: Umar's governor wrote to Umar that before us are people called the Samaritans; they read the Torah, observe the Sabbath, and do not believe in resurrection. What do you think, O Commander of the Believers, concerning their slaughtered animals? So Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to him: They are a group of the People of the Book."
"12370","From al-Thawri, from one of his companions, from al-Hakam, from Abu Iyad, concerning marrying polytheist women outside a treaty, that he disliked their women, but permitted their slaughtered animals in the land of war. As for al-Hasan ibn Umara, he mentioned it from al-Hakam, from Abu Iyad, from Ali."
"12371","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It reached me that no woman of the People of the Book is to be married except under a treaty."
"12372","From Ma'mar, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utba, from his father, he said: I was sitting with Umar beside him, when a man came and asked him about a woman and her daughter owned by his right hand, whether he may have intercourse with one of them after the other? He said: So he forbade him with a prohibition, and I wished it had been sterner than that prohibition. He said: I do not like him to uncover both of them. From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah, from his father, the same."
"12373","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, that Abd al-Rahman disliked (combining) a slave woman and her daughter in right-hand possession."
"12374","From Ma'mar and Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisa ibn Dhuayb, that a man asked Uthman about two sisters combined together? Uthman said: One verse made them lawful, and one verse made them unlawful; as for me, I do not like to do that. He said: So he left him and met a man of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him about that, and he said: As for me, I forbid you; and if any of the matter were up to me, then I found anyone doing that, I would make him an example. Ibn Shihab said: I think it was Ali."
"12375","From Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi', he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, when a man asked him about combining two sisters from those the right hand possesses, and he said: One verse forbade them both, and another verse permitted them both."
"12376","Ibn Jurayj and al-Aslami reported from Abu al-Zinad, from Abdullah ibn Niyar al-Aslami, that his father took a slave girl of his as a concubine, called Lu'lu'a, and his slave girl had a small daughter. He said: When the girl grew up he left her mother and desired her, and remained so until the girl grew up, then he wanted to take her as a concubine, so he spoke to Uthman about that during his caliphate, and he said: I neither command you nor forbid you that, and I would not do that myself. Niyar then said: Nor I; by Allah, I will not do what you do not do in that matter. So he sold the girl for six hundred dinars and did not have intercourse with her. Abu al-Zinad said: Then Amir al-Sha'bi narrated to me from Ali ibn Abi Talib that he gave fatwa with this same."
"12377","Ibn Jurayj reported: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka reporting that Mu'adh ibn Ubaydillah ibn Ma'mar came to Aisha, Mother of the Believers, and said to her: I have a concubine I have had, and she has a grown daughter, a slave girl; may I take her daughter as a concubine? She said: No. He said: Did Allah forbid her? She said: None of my family does it, nor anyone who obeys me. He said: By Allah, I will not leave her unless you say: Allah forbade her. She said: None of my family does it, nor anyone who obeys me. And a man asked Ibn Umar about that, and he said the like of Aisha's saying. He said: And I did not hear that from Aisha, but those of Banu Tamim whom you wish informed me of it."
"12378","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Qabisa ibn Dhuayb al-Aslami informed me that he asked Uthman for a fatwa about a woman and her sister from those the right hand possesses, and Uthman said: One verse permitted them both, and one verse forbade them both, and I would not do that."
"12379","From Ma'mar, from Layth, that Ibn Umar used to dislike two sisters from those the right hand possesses. Ma'mar said: And one who heard al-Hasan disliking it also informed me."
"12380","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulayka and others, that a man asked Aisha, saying: I own an old slave woman who has grown old, and she has a daughter who has reached maturity, and he had had her mother; may I take her as a concubine? She said: No. He said: Is she unlawful? She said: I forbid you from her. He said: Is she unlawful? She said: I forbid you from her, and whoever obeys me."
"12381","From al-Thawri, from more than one of his companions, that they said: If he marries her off then there is no harm in her sister. And Ibn Umar used to dislike that, even if he had married her off."
"12382","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Ikrima, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, informed him that Ibn Abbas saw no harm in a man combining two sisters, and a woman and her daughter. And Ibn Abbas used to say: Their kinship between them does not forbid them to you; what forbids them to you is only the kinship between you and them. And Ibn Abbas used to say: Except what your right hands possess. Then he says: It is unrestricted. All this Amr informed me: that Ibn Abbas gave fatwa to Mu'adh ibn Ubaydillah ibn Ma'mar that he may combine two slave girls of his, two sisters, or a mother and her daughter. He said: Who informed you of that? He said: Ikrima, the freedman of Ibn Abbas; I think he said: Ibn Abi Mulayka and whomsoever you wish."
"12383","Ibn Jurayj reported: Amr also informed me that Ibn Abbas used to wonder at Ali's saying about two sisters combined together: one verse forbade them both and another verse permitted them both, saying: Except what your right hands possess, it is unrestricted."
"12384","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, that he heard Abu al-Sha'tha: Ibn Abbas's view about combining them did not please him."
"12385","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Abdullah ibn Safwan combined a woman and her daughter."
"12386","From Ibn Jurayj and Ma'mar, they both said: Ibn Tawus informed us that he used to dislike a man combining two sisters, but he used to say: If he leaves this one never touching her again, then let him have this one."
"12387","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata was asked: May a man combine two sisters, or have his slave woman then after her her mother or her daughter? He said: No, and he disliked that."
"12388","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, that Ibn Mas'ud used to dislike (combining) a slave woman and her mother. Qatada said: And a man debated Ibn Mas'ud about combining two sisters, saying: Allah has made lawful for me what my right hand possesses. So Ibn Mas'ud became angry and said to him: Your camel is of what your right hand possesses."
"12389","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: What is forbidden of free women is disliked of slave women, except the number."
"12390","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Wahb ibn Munabbih saying about the Torah: Cursed is one who looks at the private part of a woman and her daughter."
"12391","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Wahb ibn Munabbih, he said: I heard him saying: We find it written: Whoever uncovers the private part of a woman and her daughter is cursed."
"12392","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Maymun ibn Mihran, that Ibn Umar was asked about a slave woman her master has intercourse with, then he wants to have her daughter? He said: No, until he removes her from his ownership."
"12393","From al-Thawri, from more than one of his companions, that they said: If he marries her off then there is no harm in her sister. And Ibn Umar used to dislike that, even if he had married her off."
"12394","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il, from a man called Ibrahim, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, he said: Whoever looks at the private part of a woman and her daughter, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"12395","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from Wasil, the freedman of Abu Uyayna, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Whoever looks at the private part of a woman and her daughter, Allah will veil Himself from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"12396","From al-Thawri, from Mutarrif, from Abu al-Jahm, from Abu al-Akhdar al-Tamimi, from Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: Allah forbade nothing of free women except He has forbidden it of slave women, that a man should combine them; he means: exceeding four in concubines."
"12397","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, that Ibn Mas'ud said: And I dislike your slave woman as a polytheist."
"12398","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: It is not lawful for a man who bought a polytheist slave girl to have intercourse with her until she bathes, prays, and menstruates one menstruation with him."
"12399","From Ja'far ibn Sulayman, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd informed me from al-Hasan, he said: We used to raid with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when one of them got a slave girl from the fay', and wanted to have her, he ordered her to wash her clothes and bathe, then he taught her Islam and ordered her to pray, and declared her free of pregnancy by one menstruation, then he had her."
"12400","From Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Musa ibn Abi Aisha, he said: I asked Murra ibn Sharahil and Sa'id ibn Jubayr about a man who has a Magian slave girl, may he have intercourse with her? They said: No."
"12401","From al-Thawri, from Musa ibn Abi Aisha, he said: I asked them both about a man who has a Magian slave girl, may he have intercourse with her? They said: No; they are impure if they do that. From Ibn Uyayna, from Musa ibn Abi Aisha, the same, except that one of them said: No, and the other said: They are impure if they do that."
"12402","From al-Thawri, he said: As for the Sunna, he does not fall upon her until she prays, when he has declared her free of pregnancy; and if she is of the People of the Book, let him declare her free of pregnancy, then let her bathe, and let him have her."
"12403","From Abbad ibn Kathir, or another, from Layth, from Mujahid, he said: In the Sunna she removes pubic hair, takes from her hair and her nails, bathes, washes her clothes, testifies that there is no god but Allah, and prays; but if she refuses, that does not prevent him from falling upon her after he has declared her free of pregnancy."
"12404","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: He offers Islam to her; if she refuses, let him have her if he wishes, when he has declared her free of pregnancy, even if she is Magian; but he compels her to wash from major impurity."
"12405","From Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: There is no harm in a man having intercourse with his Magian slave girl."
"12406","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata was asked about a man who used to have a woman illicitly, may he marry her daughter? He said: No, for he has looked upon her mother's private part. So a man said: Was it not said: The unlawful does not forbid the lawful? He said: That is about the slave woman: he used to fornicate with her then buys her, or fornicates with a free woman then marries her; then what he did of that does not forbid."
"12407","Ibn Jurayj reported: I heard Ata saying: If he commits adultery with his wife's mother or her daughter, both become forbidden to him."
"12408","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Jurayj, and from al-Sha'bi, from Amr, from al-Hasan, he said: If a man commits adultery with his wife's mother or his wife's daughter, both become forbidden to him."
"12409","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me from his father, about a man who used to commit adultery with a woman? He does not marry her mother nor her daughter."
"12410","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, the freedman of the family of al-Aswad, that he asked Ibn al-Musayyib, Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, and Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, about a man who has a woman unlawfully, is it right for him to marry her daughter? They said: No."
"12411","From Abd al-Wahhab and Ibn Abi Sabra, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from his maternal uncle al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, he said: I asked Ibn al-Musayyib and Urwa ibn al-Zubayr about a man who commits adultery with a woman, is her daughter lawful to him? They said: The unlawful does not forbid the lawful. From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: I said to Ibn Shihab: Do you trace it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So he denied that he had narrated it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but he heard it from some people."
"12412","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'mur said to al-Sha'bi: By Allah, the unlawful never forbade the lawful at all. Al-Sha'bi said to him: Rather, if you took a jug of wine and poured it into a well of water, that water would be unlawful. He said: And al-Hasan used to say the like of al-Sha'bi's saying."
"12413","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who commits adultery with his wife's mother. He said: He overstepped from one sanctity to another sanctity, and his wife did not become forbidden to him."
"12414","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Ibn al-Musayyib, about one who commits adultery with a close relative? She becomes forbidden in every case. He said: And Ibrahim and al-Hasan said: The hadd of adultery."
"12415","From Ma'mar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever commits adultery with a close relative will not enter Paradise."
"12416","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Abdullah said: Lawful and unlawful never meet except the unlawful overcomes the lawful. Sufyan said: And that is about a man who fornicates with a woman while he has her daughter or her mother; if that happens, he parts from her."
"12417","From Ma'mar, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, he said: What was forbidden in what is lawful is forbidden in what is unlawful."
"12418","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asbahani, he said: A trustworthy one informed me from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil ibn Muqarrin, that he said: She is forbidden to him in what is lawful, so how would she not be forbidden to him in what is unlawful."
"12419","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Abu al-Sha'tha ordered me to ask Ikrima about a man who committed adultery with a woman, then saw she has a slave girl, is it right to have the slave girl? So I asked him, and he said: No."
"12420","From Uthman ibn Sa'id, from Qatada, from Imran ibn Husayn, about one who commits adultery with his wife's mother: Both have become forbidden to him."
"12421","From Ma'mar, and he was asked about Qatada, about a man who had intercourse, meaning his wife's mother: Both have become forbidden to him. Until after that it was said to him: Then he touched her intimately (without intercourse)? He said: Then it did not forbid."
"12422","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about one who commits adultery with a close relative? If he was not muhsan he is lashed a hundred, and imprisonment and exile are made severe upon him."
"12423","Ibn Jurayj reported: I was informed from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab that he was asked about a man who fornicated with a woman's mother, then wants to marry her daughter, or fornicates with her daughter then wants to marry her mother. He said: The unlawful does not forbid the lawful. Then I came to Urwa and asked him about that, and he said the like of Ibn al-Musayyib's saying."
"12424","From al-Thawri, about a man who transgresses with his wife's sister, he said: It does not spoil her for him, and there is no waiting period in adultery."
"12425","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, about a man who committed adultery with his wife's sister: He overstepped from one sanctity to another, and his wife did not become forbidden to him. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: And it reached me from Ikrima the same."
"12426","From al-Thawri, and I asked him about a man who wanted to marry a woman, then his son said to him: I have had her unlawfully, so do not approach her. He said: God willing, his son is not to be believed."
"12427","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Umm al-Hakam, that he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I committed adultery with a woman in the pre-Islamic period and her daughter. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not see that, and that is not right: that you marry a woman while you see in her daughter what you saw of her."
"12428","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata informed me, he said: Ibn Abbas used to say, about a man who commits adultery with a woman then wants to marry her, he said: Its beginning is fornication, and its end is marriage."
"12429","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: There is no harm in that; its beginning is unlawful adultery, and its end is lawful."
"12430","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Ikrima, that Ibn Abbas said, about a man who commits adultery with a woman then marries her, when they both repent he marries her; its beginning is fornication and its end is marriage; its beginning is unlawful and its end is lawful. From Ibn al-Taymi, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, the same."
"12431","From al-Thawri, from Shayba ibn Na'ama, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, about a woman a man fornicated with, then he wants to marry her? He said: Its beginning is fornication and its end is marriage, and his wealth made her lawful to him."
"12432","From Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Ibrahim ibn Maysara, from Tawus, he said: It was said to Ibn Abbas: A man has a woman unlawfully, then he marries her. He said: Then that is better; or he said: That is better."
"12433","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about a man who has a woman unlawfully, then he marries her. He said: Now it is good; he attained the lawful. He said: And Ibn Abbas said to me: And what is disliked of that? I said: He says it is such and such. He said: Then it is such."
"12434","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I know that Allah accepts repentance from them together, as He accepts it from them separately."
"12435","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me that he heard Sabba' ibn Thabit al-Zuhri saying: Mawhab ibn Rabah married a woman, and the woman had a daughter from other than Mawhab, and Mawhab had a son from other than his wife; then Mawhab's son had the woman's daughter, so that was raised to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Umar lashed Mawhab's son, and delayed the woman until she gave birth, then lashed her, and was keen to join them together, but Mawhab's son refused."
"12436","From Ma'mar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about a man who fornicates with a woman then wants to marry her. He said: There is no harm in it."
"12437","From a shaykh of the people of Medina, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab narrating from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utba, he said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about a man who committed adultery with a woman then wants to marry her. He said: There is no repentance better than marrying her; they went out from fornication to marriage."
"12438","Ubaydullah ibn Umar reported from Nafi', he said: A man came to Abu Bakr and mentioned to him that a guest of his had deflowered his sister, forcing her against herself; so he asked him and he confessed that, and Abu Bakr lashed him the hadd, exiled him a year to Fadak, and did not lash her nor exile her, because he had forced her. Then Abu Bakr married her to him, and admitted him to her."
"12439","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', he said: Ibn Umar had a slave girl, and he had a servant boy who used to enter upon her, and he insulted him. Then Ibn Umar saw him one day and said: Are you pregnant? She said: Yes. He said: From whom? She said: From so-and-so. He said: The one you insulted? She said: Yes. So Ibn Umar asked him and he denied, and he had an extra finger. So Ibn Umar said to him: What if she brings one with an extra (finger)? He said: Then it is from me. He said: So she gave birth to a boy with an extra finger. He said: So Ibn Umar lashed them both the hadd, married her to him, and freed the boy she bore."
"12440","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Ibn Mas'ud was asked about a man who commits adultery with a woman then marries her. He said: They are two adulterers as long as they stay together. He said: So it was said to Ibn Mas'ud: What if they repent? He said: And He is who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds. He said: And Ibn Mas'ud kept repeating it until we thought he saw no harm in it."
"12441","I heard Abu Hanifa narrating from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Alqama ibn Qays was asked about a man who committed adultery with a woman, is it right for him to marry her? He said: And He is who accepts repentance from His servants, the verse."
"12442","From Ma'mar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, he said: I asked Salim ibn Abdillah about a man who commits adultery with a woman then marries her. He said: Ibn Mas'ud was asked about that, and said: And He is who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons evil deeds."
"12443","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Aisha, she said: We see only two adulterers as long as they stay together. From Ibn al-Taymi, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Mas'ud and Aisha, the same."
"12444","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, he said: He has more right to her because he loves her."
"12445","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: If a man fornicates with a woman he has more right to her than others; and if a man commits adultery with a woman and she is lashed, let him marry her if he wishes; and if they both repent, marrying her is lawful to him."
"12446","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Sha'tha, he said: He has more right to her than others."
"12447","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: If they both repent, marrying them is lawful. He said: So it was said to him: What is their repentance? He said: That one of them be alone with the other and not desire it."
"12448","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: If a woman commits adultery then repentance is seen from her, marrying her is lawful."
"12449","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: If she repents and her repentance is known, she is lawful to whoever wants to marry her."
"12450","From Muhammad ibn Rashid, he said: I heard Makhul saying: It is not lawful for a Muslim man to marry a woman punished for adultery, nor is it lawful for a Muslim woman to marry a man punished for adultery; Allah only sent down this verse: The adulterer marries none but an adulteress, about this."
"12451","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, he said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas early in the day and found him fasting, then I entered upon him in that day and found him breaking his fast, so I asked him about that, and he said: I saw a slave girl of mine and she pleased me, so I had her. He said: Shall I tell you more: she had committed indecency, then we made her chaste."
"12452","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that he had intercourse with a slave girl who had fornicated. So I said to him: Do you fall upon her though she fornicated? He said: Woe to you, she is my right-hand possession."
"12453","From Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ma'bad, he said: Ibn Abbas had intercourse with Umm Sulayt after he disapproved of her pregnancy."
"12454","From Ubaydullah and Abdullah, the two sons of Umar, from Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that his father Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib had intercourse with a slave girl of his who had fornicated."
"12455","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, that Ibn Mas'ud said: I dislike a man having his slave woman as a prostitute."
"12456","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from Tawus, he said: And it reached me from al-Hasan, he said: If you see adultery from your slave girl, do not approach her; and if you see that from your wife, do not touch her, or do not keep her."
"12457","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata used to forbid a slave marrying his mistress."
"12458","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: A woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab while we were at al-Jabiya; she had married her slave; so he rebuked her and intended to stone her, and said: No Muslim is lawful to you after him."
"12459","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: A woman took a servant boy of hers as a concubine, and it was mentioned to Umar, so he asked her: What carried you to this? She said: I thought lawful for me what is lawful for men of right-hand possession. So Umar consulted the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about her, and they said: She interpreted the Book of Allah contrary to its interpretation. So Umar said: No doubt, by Allah, I will never make you lawful to a free man after him; as if he punished her with that, and he averted the hadd from her, and ordered the slave not to approach her."
"12460","From Ma'mar, from Qatada, he said: A woman came to Abu Bakr and said: Do you know I wanted to free my slave and marry him? He is lighter upon me in maintenance than others. He said: Go to Umar and ask him. So she asked Umar, and Umar beat her, I think he said, until she urinated; then he said: The Arabs will remain in good as long as their women are restrained."
"12461","From al-Thawri, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, that Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to him about a slave marrying his mistress, so he wrote forbidding that, and threatening about it."
"12462","From Abu Bakr ibn Abdillah, that he heard his father saying: I attended Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz; an Arab woman came to him with a Roman servant boy of hers, saying: I took him as a concubine, but my cousins prevented me; I am but at the station of a man who has a slave girl and has intercourse with her, so restrain my cousins from me. So Umar said to her: Did you marry before him? She said: Yes. He said: By Allah, were it not for your place of ignorance I would have stoned you with stones; but take him and sell him to one who takes him out to a land other than her land."
"12463","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who married his sister to a servant boy of his, he said: If she has a guardian other than him who permits the marriage, otherwise not."
"12464","From al-Thawri, about a man who marries his slave woman to his servant boy, he said: She should not see anything of her master, nor should he see anything of her. From more than one."
"12465","From Ma'mar, about a man who marries his slave woman to his servant boy, he said: It is disliked to look at her private part."
"12466","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ata, he said: I said to him: May a woman's servant boy see her head and her foot? He said: I do not like that, unless he is a small boy; as for a grown man of awe, no."
"12467","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: A woman does not put off the head-cover before her husband's servant boy."
"12468","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Tawus and Mujahid, they both said: A slave does not look at his mistress's hair. He said: In some recitation: And what your right hands possess, those who have not reached puberty."
"12469","Ibn Jurayj reported: Isma'il ibn Kathir informed me from his grandmother, she said: I was sitting with Ama, daughter of Abd ibn Amr, sister of Dhu al-Yadayn, and with her was Abdullah ibn Umar; then nothing startled Abdullah ibn Umar but a servant boy of Ama's, called Rukana, entering without permission. So he said: Who is this? Ama said: A servant boy of mine. He said: Go out, may you have no mother, and seek permission, saying: Peace upon you, may I enter? So the boy did so."
"12470","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: There is no harm in a man looking at a woman's forelock from under the head-cover, if he is a mahram; as for her casting off her head-cover before him, no."
"12471","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a woman who removes her headscarf in front of a mahram relative: he said: As for seeing something from beneath the headscarf, there is no harm, but as for her removing the headscarf, then no."
"12472","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father: he said: Nothing was more disliked by him than seeing the private area of a mahram female relative; he said: And he used to dislike that she remove her headscarf in front of him."
"12473","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from Tawus, that he used to dislike seeing the hair of his daughter; Layth said: And al-Sha'bi used to dislike that from every mahram female relative."
"12474","From al-Thawri, from Salim, from Abu Ya'la: he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah used to attend to his mother, meaning he would comb her hair. [source partly garbled]"
"12475","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, about this verse: or their sons or their husbands' sons: he said: They may look at what is above the forearm, and the head, and the ear."
"12476","Ibn Jurayj reported: I knew Ata to see no harm in a slave taking a concubine from his wealth, or he said: his master permitting him with his permission."
"12477","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi: he said: Ibn Umar used to allow his slaves to take concubines, and did not criticize them for that."
"12478","From Ma'mar: he said: When a man frees a slave of his who has a concubine, and frees them both together, then he should not approach her except through marriage."
"12479","From al-Thawri, from Qays ibn Muslim, from al-Sha'bi: he said: A slave may take as many concubines as he wishes; and Yunus reported the same from al-Hasan."
"12480","From Hisham, from Ibn Sirin: he disliked that a slave take a concubine."
"12481","From al-Thawri: he said: Ibn Sirin and al-Hakam ibn Utaybah disliked it; al-Thawri said: And we hold this view: her private part is not lawful to two men."
"12482","From al-Thawri: A slave may claim his young daughter if he takes a concubine from his master's wealth; from Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab disliked it. [wording ambiguous]"
"12483","Ibn Jurayj reported: Amr ibn Dinar told me that Abu Ma'bad, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, told him that a slave belonging to Ibn Abbas had a wife who was a slavegirl belonging to Ibn Abbas, and he divorced her irrevocably; Ibn Abbas said: You have no divorce, so take her back, but he refused; then Ibn Abbas said: She is yours, so make her lawful to you through ownership, but he refused."
"12484","From Ma'mar, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: he said: There is no harm in a slave taking a concubine."
"12485","From Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar saw no harm in it, and that he freed a slave boy of his who had two concubines, freeing them all together, and said: Do not approach them except through marriage; and Ibn Jurayj also reported it to us from Nafi."
"12486","From Ma'mar, from al-Hasan: he said: When a man permits a slavegirl to a man, and he frees her for him, then if she becomes pregnant the child is attributed to him."
"12487","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Umar said: It is not lawful for you to tread a private part except a private part which, if you wish you may sell, and if you wish you may give away, and if you wish you may free."
"12488","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb: he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: My mother had a slavegirl, and she permitted her to me to approach her; he said: She is not lawful to you except by one of three: either you marry her, or you buy her, or she gives her to you."
"12489","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who permits a slavegirl to a man: he said: If he has intercourse with her he is flogged one hundred lashes, whether previously married or not; if she becomes pregnant the child is not attributed to him and does not inherit from him, but he may ransom it; they have no right to prevent him."
"12490","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: Ata told me: he said: It used to be done: a man would permit his slavegirl to his slave boy, and his son, and his brother, and his father, and a woman to her husband, but I do not like that this be done, and nothing firm has reached me about it; and it has reached me that a man would send his slavegirl to his guest."
"12491","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Bakr told me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zadawayh, from Tawus, that he said: She is more lawful than food; if she gives birth, her child belongs to the one to whom she was permitted, while she belongs to her first master."
"12492","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: Amr ibn Dinar told me that he heard Tawus say: Ibn Abbas said: When a man's wife, or his daughter, or his sister permits her slavegirl to him, he may have intercourse with her while she still belongs to her; Ibn Abbas said: Let him place it between her thighs."
"12493","From Ma'mar: he said: It was said to Amr ibn Dinar: Tawus sees no harm in it? He said: Private parts are not to be loaned."
"12494","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: Ibn Tawus told me, from his father: he saw no harm; he said: It is lawful, and if she gives birth her child is free, and the slavegirl belongs to his wife, and her husband owes nothing."
"12495","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: Abdullah ibn Qays told me, from al-Walid ibn Hisham who told him, that he asked Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, saying: His wife permitted her slavegirl to her son? He said: Then she belongs to him."
"12496","From Ma'mar, from Amr, from al-Hasan, and Ibn Mujahid, from his father: he said: When she permits her to him, then he frees her for him, and the child is attributed to him."
"12497","Ibn Jurayj reported: I said to Ata: A man who takes his slavegirl while she is with his slave? He said: He is made an example of but not given the fixed punishment."
"12498","Ibn Jurayj reported: I heard Ata and others narrating that [lacuna in source], and he said: By Allah, if you admitted that I would have stoned you; Ata and others said: He would not have stoned him, but he separated them. [source truncated]"
"12499","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, that Umar said to a man from Thaqif - others besides Ayyub said he was al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah - he said: Umar said to him: What did your home-born slave boy do? He said: That is when Umar called him and asked him about him, and he said: Good, O Commander of the Faithful, and I have married him off; he said: Perhaps you visit his wife when he is away? He said: No, O Commander of the Faithful; he said: If you had told me that you do that, I would have made you an example; he said: And it reached me that Ali advised him not to confess."
"12500","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, that a man among them had intercourse with his slavegirl while she was with his slave, so Umar ibn al-Khattab flogged him one hundred lashes."
"12501","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who takes his slavegirl while she is with his slave: he said: He is flogged one hundred lashes."
"12502","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Ubayd asking Ata about a man who married his slavegirl to a slave of his, and she bore him children, then the master claimed some of her children; he said: He has no claim; the child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone."
"12503","Ibn Jurayj reported: Musa ibn Uqbah told me, from Nafi, that a man from Thaqif told him that a man among them had a beautiful slavegirl whom Umar knew; the man married her to a slave boy of his, while the man continued to have intercourse with her; the slave came to Umar and told him that; Umar hid the slave and sent for his master and asked him: What happened to so-and-so? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, she is with me, and I have married her to a slave boy of mine; Umar said: Do you have intercourse with her? Those with Umar signaled to him to say No, so he said No; he said: By Allah, if you had told me that you do that, I would have made you an example for the people."
"12504","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a woman and her husband who own a slavegirl who has a husband, and the woman's husband has intercourse with the slavegirl: he said: If he had not divorced her - or he said: It is my son, then the child is his - the child belongs to the marriage bed, and the adulterer gets the stone; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed so; but if the slave had divorced her and the master had intercourse with her during her waiting period, the physiognomists are called; Urwah ibn al-Zubayr told me that Umar ibn al-Khattab called the physiognomists in the case of two men who both claimed the child of a woman with whom they had intercourse in one purity period; and if the master had intercourse with her after the waiting period ended, the child belongs to her master; and he mentioned exemplary punishment."
"12505","From Ibn Jurayj, about a man who married his slavegirl to his slave for ten dirhams, then freed them both together: he said: The master takes nothing from her dowry, because it is his wealth, and there is no debt upon his slave, nor does he take anything from the slave; he said: There is no harm in marrying his slave to his slavegirl with witnesses but assigning her no dowry, but if he married his virgin slavegirl then freed her, her dowry belongs to her master."
"12506","From al-Thawri, about a man who married a slavegirl then bought her before consummating with her: he said: He does not give her family her dowry, for that came about from their side; but if he consummated with her, the dowry belongs to the one who sold her."
"12507","From al-Thawri, about a man who married off his slavegirl for a known deferred dowry, then her master freed her: he said: The dowry belongs to the master, because it became due when it did, while she belonged to him."
"12508","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim: he said: When her master frees her before he consummates with her; Ibn Shubrumah said: The dowry belongs to the master."
"12509","From al-Thawri, about an authorized slave trader who had a slave wife, then bought her: he said: The marriage is not invalidated, because ownership belongs to another, and if the slave wishes he may sell her."
"12510","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: he said: The waiting period of a slavegirl is one menstruation."
"12511","From Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Maymun ibn Mihran, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The divorce of a slavegirl is two divorces, and her waiting period is two menstruations."
"12512","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of Talhah's family, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab: he said: A slave marries two wives and divorces twice, and a slavegirl waits two menstruations; if she does not menstruate, then two months - or he said: a month and a half."
"12513","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Utbah: he said: A slave marries two, and the waiting period of a slavegirl is two menstruations."
"12514","Ibn Jurayj reported: Amr ibn Dinar told me that Amr ibn Aws told him, from a man from Thaqif, from Umar, that he said: If I could, I would make the waiting period of a slavegirl one and a half menstruations; Qatadah said: A man stood and said: Then make it a month and a half, O Commander of the Faithful, and he fell silent."
"12515","Ibn Jurayj reported: Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: Umar assigned her two menstruations."
"12516","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah: both said: The waiting period of a divorced slavegirl is two menstruations; he said: And Qatadah attributed it to Ibn al-Musayyib."
"12517","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: I said to Ata: The waiting period of a slavegirl? He said: Two menstruations; he said: They mentioned that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: If I could, I would make it one and a half menstruations."
"12518","From Dawud ibn Qays: he said: I asked Salim ibn Abdullah about the waiting period of a slavegirl; he said: Two menstruations, and if she does not menstruate, then a month and a half."
"12519","From Ma'mar, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Mas'ud: he said: She bears half the punishment, but she does not get half the concession."
"12520","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin: he said: I do not see the waiting period of a slavegirl except like that of a free woman, unless a sunnah has established otherwise, for the sunnah is more deserving to be followed."
"12521","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: I said to Ata: A slavegirl belonging to a slave - he divorces her once, then she is freed after observing one menstruation, and she chooses to leave; he said: She observes the waiting period of a free woman, counting what passed of her waiting period as a slavegirl; and Amr ibn Dinar said the same - whether irrevocably divorced or not; he said: And Ibn Abi Layla reported from their elders the same as Umar's view."
"12522","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, about a slavegirl whom a slave divorces once, then she menstruates once, then is freed and chooses her husband: she observes the waiting period of a free woman, counting that menstruation, unless her husband had taken her back; if he divorced her twice, then she was freed during the waiting period, she also observes the waiting period of a free woman; Qatadah said: If he wishes he may take her back during the waiting period, and she remains with him on the basis of one divorce; al-Zuhri said: She is not lawful until she marries another husband."
"12523","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, and Yunus, from al-Hasan, about a slavegirl under a man who divorces her once, then freedom reaches her during the waiting period: both said: She observes three menstrual cycles; if he divorced her twice and freedom reached her during the waiting period, she observes two menstruations."
"12524","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata said: Three merchants passed around a slavegirl and she gave birth; Umar called the physiognomists, and they attributed her child to one of them; then Umar said: Whoever buys a slavegirl who has reached menstruation, let him wait with her until she menstruates; if she has not reached menstruation, then forty-five days."
"12525","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, about the waiting period of a young or menopaused slavegirl? He said: Umar said: A month and a half."
"12526","From Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata: he said: Forty-five nights."
"12527","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyib: he said: The waiting period of a young slavegirl, or one who has stopped menstruating, is a month and a half."
"12528","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri: he said: Her waiting period is two months, a month for each menstruation."
"12529","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Basri, from Mujahid: he said: Three months."
"12530","From Ibn Abi Shaybah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim: he said: Three months."
"12531","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan: he said: Three months."
"12532","From al-Thawri, from al-Hasan: he said: Three months."
"12533","From Ma'mar, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar: he said: I disputed to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz about a slavegirl who did not menstruate, and he set her waiting period at three months; Ma'mar said: I only know him to have said: He placed her in the care of a man for three months."
"12534","From Ma'mar: he said: One who heard al-Hasan say informed me: Three months."
"12535","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: I said to Ata: The waiting period of a slavegirl sold who has menstruated? He said: One menstruation; and Amr said: One menstruation."
"12536","Ibn Jurayj reported: Ata said: Three merchants passed around a slavegirl, and she gave birth; Umar ibn al-Khattab called the physiognomists, and they attributed her child to one of them; then Umar said: Whoever buys a slavegirl who has reached menstruation, let him wait with her until she menstruates, and if she has not menstruated, let him wait with her forty-five nights."
"12537","From al-Thawri, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud: he said: A slavegirl is cleared of pregnancy with one menstruation."
"12538","From Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cleared Safiyyah of pregnancy with one menstruation."
"12539","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he used to set the waiting period of a slavegirl sold at one menstruation."
"12540","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, about a slavegirl sold: he said: She is cleared with one menstruation."
"12541","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a slavegirl sold who has menstruated: he said: She is cleared with one menstruation; Ma'mar said: And one who heard al-Hasan informed me he said the same."
"12542","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a slavegirl sold who has menstruated: he said: The one who sold her clears her, and the one who bought her clears her with another menstruation; al-Thawri said so too."
"12543","From Ma'mar, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Tawus: he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a caller in one of his campaigns: No man should have intercourse with a pregnant woman, nor with a non-pregnant one, until she menstruates."
"12544","From al-Thawri, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi: he said: The Muslims captured women on the day of Awtas, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them not to have intercourse with a pregnant one until she gives birth, nor with a non-pregnant one until she menstruates one menstruation."
"12545","From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, about a slavegirl bought while menstruating: he said: That menstruation suffices her; al-Thawri said: Others said: It does not suffice her until she is cleared with another menstruation."
"12546","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: he said: When a slavegirl was a virgin he would not clear her; Ma'mar said: And Ayyub said: He clears her before having intercourse with her."
"12547","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a virgin slavegirl a man buys from a woman: he said: He does not clear her, but if he buys her from a man he clears her."
"12548","From Ma'mar, from a man: he said: Al-Hakam ibn Utaybah was asked about a virgin slavegirl sold - is her womb cleared? He said: Yes, she is cleared. It was said: Then why is a free woman not cleared when she marries? He said: A free woman is trusted with what a slavegirl is not trusted with."
"12549","From al-Thawri, about a slavegirl who has not reached puberty: he said: She is cleared as an old woman is cleared: if she was given as a gift, or given in charity to him, or he inherited her, he clears her; even if she was not in his possession and he obtained her exclusively, he clears her."
"12550","From Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad: he said: Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir told me, from Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while at Khaybar, a woman passed by him who was visibly pregnant, and he said: To whom does she belong? It was said: To so-and-so; he said: Does he perhaps have intercourse with her? They said: Yes; he said: Then how will he deal with her child? Will he make him inherit though he is not his son, or will he enslave him though he feeds him in his hearing and sight? I had intended to curse him with a curse that would enter the grave with him."
"12551","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid: he said: Semen increases the child."
"12552","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to have intercourse following a pregnancy not from him; he said: And he forbade selling war booty until it is divided."
"12553","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ata, about a man who married off his slavegirl whom he used to have intercourse with: he said: Her waiting period is two menstruations after he marries her off."
"12554","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah: he said: Two menstruations."
"12555","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri: he said: He clears her with one menstruation."
"12556","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri: he said: When a man has intercourse with his slavegirl, her waiting period is three months."
"12557","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: I said to Ata: A man married his milk-sister, and a woman married off her slavegirl? He said: She observes a waiting period. I said: From what? He said: They were both slavegirls."
"12558","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, about a man who buys a slavegirl and clears her: he may kiss and embrace during her clearance."
"12559","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from al-Hasan: he said: He may enjoy what is short of the private part."
"12560","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim: he said: He may enjoy what is short of the private part."
"12561","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin: he said: He should not kiss nor embrace."
"12562","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin: he said: He should not kiss nor embrace; and this is also Ayyub's view."
"12563","From al-Thawri: he said: We hold the view of Ibn Sirin: he should not kiss nor embrace."
"12564","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who has intercourse with his slavegirl and she does not bear him a child, then he dies leaving her: she is cleared with two months and five nights."
"12565","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, about a slavegirl her master has intercourse with, and she did not bear him a child: he said: When her master who had intercourse with her frees her, she observes three months."
"12566","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, about a man who grants a slavegirl he had intercourse with deferred freedom upon his death, then dies: she observes three menstrual cycles; and Amr said so too."
"12567","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Amr ibn al-As said about a slavegirl freed after death, whose master used to have intercourse with her: if she did not bear him a child, her waiting period when he dies leaving her is four months and ten days."
"12568","From al-Thawri: he said: A mudabbarah observes three menstrual cycles."
"12569","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, about a man who frees his pregnant concubine: she observes three menstrual cycles; he said: She is a free woman; and Amr ibn Dinar said so."
"12570","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: he said: She observes one menstruation."
"12571","From al-Thawri, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim, and Ma'mar, from Abu Hashim, from Ibrahim: he said: When a concubine is freed, or her master dies leaving her, she observes three menstrual cycles."
"12572","From Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ali: he said: The waiting period of a concubine is three menstrual cycles."
"12573","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri: he said: An umm al-walad observes, when her master dies leaving her, four months and ten days."
"12574","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Ibn al-Musayyib: he said: She observes four months and ten days."
"12575","From Ma'mar, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr: he said: An umm al-walad observes, when her master dies leaving her, four months and ten days."
"12576","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: he said: She observes one menstruation."
"12577","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn An'am, from Rashid ibn al-Harith, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about an umm al-walad: Her child frees her, and she observes the waiting period of a free woman."
"12578","From al-Thawri, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Umar: he said: She observes one menstruation."
"12579","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il, that al-Sha'bi said: She observes one menstruation."
"12580","From Abdullah ibn Kathir, from Yunus, from al-Hasan: he said: When she is freed, her waiting period is one menstruation."
"12581","From al-Thawri, about an umm al-walad whom her master married off, then her husband died before consummating with her, so she observed a waiting period, then returned to her master, then he died leaving her: she must observe a waiting period; had her master died while she was in her husband's waiting period, it would have sufficed her."
"12582","From al-Thawri, about an umm al-walad whom her master married off, whose husband did not consummate with her until her master died, then her husband left her before consummating: she owes no waiting period, neither from the master nor from the husband."
"12583","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, about a man who frees his pregnant concubine? He said: She observes three menstrual cycles; he said: She is a free woman; Amr ibn Dinar said so."
"12584","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib: he said: Uthman judged about a mukatab who divorced his wife twice, while she was free: he judged that she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband."
"12585","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: I said to Ata: How many times does a slave divorce a free woman? He said: Some people say: Waiting period and divorce follow the women; others say: Divorce follows the men, whoever they are, and waiting period follows the women, whoever they are. I said: Which is more pleasing to you? He said: Divorce follows the men, and waiting period follows the women."
"12586","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Uthman ibn Affan and Zayd ibn Thabit said: Divorce follows the men, and waiting period follows the women; Abu Salamah mentioned it from Nufay, the mukatab of Umm Salamah."
"12587","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Zayd ibn Thabit and Uthman ibn Affan said about a slave belonging to Umm Salamah named Nufay, who divorced his wife twice: she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband, though his wife was free."
"12588","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ayyub: he said: Raja ibn Haywah narrated to me, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from A'ishah, Mother of the Believers: he said: A slave boy of hers under whom was a free wife came to her and said to her: I divorced my wife; A'ishah said: Do not approach her; go and ask; Uthman was asked and said: Do not approach her; then he came to A'ishah and told her, then he went to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him, and he said: Do not approach her."
"12589","From al-Thawri, from Abu al-Zinad, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that a mukatab belonging to Umm Salamah named Nufay had a wife under him, and he divorced her twice, then wanted to take her back; the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to go to Uthman and ask him about that; he met him at the stairs holding the hand of Zayd ibn Thabit, and asked them both, and they both hastened to answer him: She is forbidden to you until she marries another husband besides you; except that al-Thawri said: He met them while they were walking hand on waist."
"12590","From Ibn Jurayj: I was told, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: Divorce follows the men, whoever they are, and waiting period follows the women, whoever they are."
"12591","From Ibn Jurayj and al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyib: he said: Divorce follows the men, and waiting period follows the women."
"12592","Ibn Jurayj reported: he said: Abdullah ibn Ziyad ibn Sam'an wrote to me that Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari told him, from Nafi, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a slave boy of hers divorced his wife twice, so Umm Salamah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ruling, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is forbidden to him until she marries another husband; Abd al-Razzaq said: And I myself asked Abdullah ibn Ziyad ibn Sam'an, that Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari told him, from Nafi, from Umm Salamah, then he mentioned the same."
"12593","From al-Thawri, from Ash'ath, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Mas'ud: he said: Divorce and waiting period follow the woman."
"12594","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim: he said: Divorce and waiting period follow the woman."
"12595","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Ali said: The sunnah follows the woman - meaning divorce - and waiting period follows her; Ma'mar said: And one who heard al-Hasan informed me he says the same."
"12596","From Ibrahim ibn Abi Yahya, and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, and others, from Isa, from al-Sha'bi, about twelve of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): they said: Divorce and waiting period follow the woman."
"12597","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: he said: Whichever of the two is enslaved, divorce is reduced by his enslavement, and waiting period follows the women."
"12598","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: he said: Whichever of the two is enslaved, divorce is reduced by his enslavement, and waiting period follows the women."
"12599","From Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: he said: Whichever of the two is enslaved, divorce is reduced by his enslavement, and waiting period follows the woman - meaning: when a slavegirl is under a free man and he divorces her, her divorce is two, and her waiting period is two menstruations; and if a free woman is under a slave, her divorce is two, and her waiting period is three menstrual cycles."
"12600","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Ata, that Ibn Abbas used to say: The divorce of a slave is in his master's hand: if he divorces, it is valid, and if he separates, it is one - when both belong to him; and when the slave belongs to him and the slavegirl belongs to another, he divorces on behalf of the master if he wishes."
"12601","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: Amr ibn Dinar told me: he said: More than one told me: they used to say: A slave has no divorce except with his master's permission."
"12602","Ibn Jurayj reported, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Abu Ma'bad told him that a slave belonging to Ibn Abbas had a wife who was a slavegirl belonging to Ibn Abbas, and he divorced her irrevocably; Ibn Abbas said: You have no divorce, take her back, but he refused."
"12603","Ma'mar reported, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, that a slave asked Ibn Umar, and he said: Do not return to her, even if your head is struck."
"12604","Ibn Jurayj reported: he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say about a slave and slavegirl: Their master joins them and separates them."
"12605","Ibn Jurayj reported: he said: Amr ibn Dinar told me, from Abu al-Sha'tha, that he said: A slave has no divorce except with his master's permission: if he divorces twice, his master may not allow it if he wishes; Abu al-Sha'tha says so."
"12606","Ma'mar reported, from Ayyub: he said: I said to Sa'id ibn Jubayr: Jabir ibn Zayd says about a slave's divorce: His divorce is in his master's hand; Sa'id said: Jabir lied; divorce belongs to the one who mounts the woman."
"12607","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib: he said: When a master marries off his slave, he has no right to separate them; Ma'mar said: And Hisham ibn Urwah told me: he said: We asked him about a man who married his slave to a woman - may he take her away without her willing consent? He said: No; but if he bought him after another had married him off, then he has more right: if he wishes he separates them, and if he wishes he leaves them."
"12608","From Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: he said: When a master permits his slave to marry, no divorce of his wife is valid except the slave divorces her; as for taking the slavegirl of his male slave, or the slavegirl of his female slave, there is no harm in it."
"12609","My father told me, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Shurayh, that he used to allow a slave's divorce but not his marriage; and its explanation is: he may not marry except with his master's permission, but once he marries, divorce is in the slave's hand."
"12610","From Ma'mar: he said: A slave's divorce is valid; Ma'mar said: From a man, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, that he said: When his master marries him off, divorce is in the slave's hand."
"12611","From al-Thawri, from a man who was a hireling of Salim ibn Abdullah, from Salim ibn Abdullah: he said: Umar said: When a slave marries without his masters' permission, his marriage is unlawful; when he marries with his masters' permission, divorce is in the hands of the one who makes the private part lawful."
"12612","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that a man married his slave to his slavegirl, then placed in his hand authority to divorce her; Ibn al-Musayyib said: Evil is what he did."
"12613","From al-Thawri: he said: When you marry off your slavegirl, you have no right to take her away from her husband."
"12614","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: I said to Ata: May I take my slavegirl away from a slave of another people to whom I married her? He said: Yes, and satisfy him. I said: He refuses except keeping her dowry. He said: It is all his; if he refuses, take her away if you wish; and from a free man if you married her to him - then he later retracted that and said: Do not take her away from a free man, even if you give him the dowry; do not employ her, nor sell her, nor take her away."
"12615","From Ibn Jurayj: he said: I said to Ata: May her master take her away wrongfully without need? He said: Yes, but he sins."
"12616","From al-Thawri, from a man who was a hired worker of Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Salim, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: When the slave marries without the permission of his masters, his marriage is unlawful, and when he marries with the permission of his masters, then divorce is in the hand of the one who makes the private part lawful."
"12617","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man married without the permission of his master, then divorced while his master did not know. He said: His marriage is not valid, that is not a marriage, nor is his divorce a divorce. Ata said: But he has missed the Sunnah."
"12618","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: There is no marriage for a slave except with the permission of his master. And Qatadah mentioned it from al-Hasan."
"12619","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any slave who marries without the permission of his master is a fornicator."
"12620","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar flogged a slave boy of his with the hadd punishment when he married without his permission, and he separated between them."
"12621","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar found a slave of his who had married without his permission, so he separated between them, nullified his dower, and flogged him with the hadd."
"12622","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to consider the marriage of the slave without the permission of his master to be fornication, and he held that the hadd is upon him, and upon the woman he married if he had intercourse with her and she knew he was a slave, and those who married them off are to be punished."
"12623","From al-Thawri, he said: Salamah ibn Tammam informed me, from a man, concerning a slave who married without the permission of his masters, he said: She has made her private part lawful."
"12624","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: A slave boy belonging to Abu Musa married a woman and drove to her five young she-camels as dower, then the case was brought to Uthman, so he annulled the marriage, gave her two young she-camels, and returned three to Abu Musa."
"12625","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, concerning a slave who married without the permission of his master, he said: If the master wishes he separates between them, and if he wishes he leaves them together in their marriage. From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, the same as the saying of al-Hasan."
"12626","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: He divorced his wife with the permission of her master, making it final, then he freed her. He said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. And al-Thawri said it."
"12627","From Mamar, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, he said concerning it: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband; she becomes lawful only from the same door by which she was made unlawful."
"12628","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Amr ibn Muttab, from al-Hasan, freedman of Ibn Nawfal, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a slave who divorced his wife twice, then he freed her, can he marry her? He said: Yes. It was said: From whom is this? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave fatwa to that effect."
"12629","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I said to Ata: A man finally divorced a slave woman, then bought her, while she had not married anyone after him, is she lawful for him? He said: Yes, Ibn Abbas used to say it. Ata said: And if he had intercourse with her when he bought her, then freed her, let him marry her before she marries another husband, but if he did not have intercourse with her, then no."
"12630","From al-Thawri, he said: Uthman ibn Hakim informed me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that a slave girl of Kathir ibn al-Salt was under a slave, then he separated from her finally, then it was decreed for him that he should free, so he wanted to buy her, and Zayd ibn Thabit said: She is not lawful for you until she marries a husband other than you."
"12631","From Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Zayd ibn Thabit, concerning the slave woman whose husband divorces her finally, then he buys her, that she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. Malik said it, and Ibn al-Musayyib and Sulayman ibn Yasar said it."
"12632","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that Kathir, freedman of al-Salt, divorced his wife twice, then bought her, and he asked Zayd ibn Thabit about her, and he said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"12633","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayyah informed me, from Qusayd and another man, that Zayd ibn Thabit said concerning a man who finally divorced a slave woman, then bought her and freed her, Zayd said: If he had intercourse with her when he bought her, then freed her, he shall not marry her until she marries another husband. Ibn Jurayj said: The name of the slave was Qistas, the slave boy of Kathir ibn al-Salt."
"12634","From Mamar, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ibn Qusayd, that Kathir, freedman of al-Salt, had divorced her twice, then bought her and freed her, so Zayd said: If you had intercourse with her by ownership it would have become lawful for you, but she is not lawful for you until she marries a husband other than you."
"12635","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying concerning the slave woman who is under a man, then he divorces her, then buys her after that and takes her as a concubine, he said: I dislike that."
"12636","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, that he was asked about a slave woman who was under a man, then he divorced her twice, then bought her, he said: She is not lawful for him except from the door by which she was made unlawful to him."
"12637","From al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, he said: She is not lawful for him."
"12638","From al-Thawri, from Ismail, he said: Al-Shabi was asked: What do you think, if her master had intercourse with her? He said: He is not a husband."
"12639","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me that a slave from the people of Yemen divorced his wife finally, then the slave wanted to buy her, so he came to Ibn Abbas asking him about that, and he ordered him to buy her if he wished."
"12640","From Shubah, from Abu Awn, from Abu Salih, from Ali, concerning a man who had a slave woman, then divorced her twice, then bought her, he said: It was said to him: May he approach her? And he refused."
"12641","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: When the slave woman is freed while with a slave, she is given the choice; if she chooses herself it is one pronouncement, otherwise it is nothing."
"12642","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: When she chooses herself it is one irrevocable pronouncement. Mamar said, and Ishaq ibn Rashid informed me that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: It is an irrevocable divorce."
"12643","From Mamar, from Hammad, he said: If she chooses herself it is a separation and not a divorce. And al-Thawri mentioned it from Mansur, from Ibrahim, and from Layth, from Tawus."
"12644","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, he said: If she wishes she stays with him, and if she wishes she leaves him. And Hasan ibn Muslim and others said so."
"12645","From al-Zuhri, he said: Barirah came to Aishah seeking help in her contract of emancipation, so Aishah said: What do you think, if I count out to them what they ask of you in one payment, will they sell you to me so I free you? She said: Until I ask them. So she went and asked them, and they said: Yes, but the wala is for us. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to her, and she mentioned that to him, so he said: Buy her and free her, for wala belongs to the one who frees. So she bought her and freed her. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood as a preacher and said: What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah, that condition of his is void, even if he stipulates a hundred conditions. The condition of Allah is more rightful and more binding."
"12646","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah saying: When Aishah bargained for Barirah, she said: Free her, and they said: But you must stipulate wala for us. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came in, and she said that to him, so he said: Yes, stipulate it, for wala belongs to the one who frees. Then he stood and addressed, and said: What is the matter with a stipulation before which the right of Allah has already come? Wala belongs to the one who frees."
"12647","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr saying: A slave girl of Banu Hilal called Barirah came seeking help from Aishah in her contract of emancipation, so Aishah bargained with her people for her, and they said: We will not sell her except with wala for us. So she left her and said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: They refused to sell her except with wala for them. He said: That should not prevent you, wala belongs only to the one who frees. So Aishah bought her and freed her, then Barirah was given the choice and she chose herself. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, apportioned a sheep for her, and she gave half of it to Aishah as a gift. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you have any food? She said: No, except this sheep which you gave Barirah. He looked for a while, then said: It has reached its proper place; for her it is charity, and for us it is a gift. So he ate from it. And Urwah said: She bought her as a mukatabah for eight uqiyyahs, and she had not yet paid anything of her contract."
"12648","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: Barirah gave to Aishah something of charity that had been given to her in charity. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to her, she mentioned it to him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: It is charity for her, and a gift for us."
"12649","Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: That the husband of Barirah was a slave of some people of the Ansar called Mughith. By Allah, it is as if I am looking at him coming following her in the streets of Madinah while he weeps."
"12650","Then Ayyub said: From Ibn Sirin: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke to Barirah about returning to her husband. She said: O Messenger of Allah, do you command me with that? He said: I am only an intercessor for him. She said: No, by Allah, I will never return to him."
"12651","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Barirah observed waiting period of three menstruations."
"12652","From al-Thawri, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, he said: There was a slave called Mughith. And another besides Khalid said: He followed her in the streets, his eyes flowing with tears."
"12653","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: She is not given the choice unless she is with a slave. From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the same."
"12654","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning a slave woman freed while with a slave, then she does not choose until her husband has intercourse with her, they said: There is no choice for her. Mamar said, and Ayyub informed me, from Abu Qilabah, and from Nafi, the same."
"12655","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When he has intercourse with her, there is no choice for her."
"12656","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that a freedwoman of Banu Adi ibn Kab called Zabra told him that she was with a slave, then she was freed. She said: Hafsah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to me saying: I shall inform you of a matter, and I do not like you to do anything: Your affair is in your hand until your husband touches you; when he touches you, you have nothing. She said: I said: It is divorce, it is divorce, it is divorce. As for Ibn Uyaynah, he mentioned it from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Zabra."
"12657","From Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar said: She has the choice before her husband has intercourse with her; if she affirms him and he has intercourse with her, then he may not separate from her except if he wishes."
"12658","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If he had intercourse with her before knowing that she has the choice, then she has the choice when she learns. But if she knew she has the choice, then he had intercourse with her, she has no choice."
"12659","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: If he had intercourse with her while she knew, she has no choice. If he had intercourse with her while she did not know, she has the choice when she learns, even if he had intercourse with her a thousand times, until upright witnesses testify that she knew she has the choice."
"12660","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: If she is freed while her husband is a slave, and he hastens to her and has intercourse with her before she knows she has the choice, she has the choice when she learns. And if I were in charge I would have flogged him with a beating that would lame his shoulders."
"12661","From al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: When he has intercourse with her after she knows she has the choice, she has no choice."
"12662","From al-Thawri, he said: When she is freed, meaning while she has a husband, and she is in a gathering, and she knows she has the choice, and she does not choose in that gathering until she stands, she has no choice. If she claims she did not know, she is made to swear an oath, then she is given the choice. Sufyan said: And some people say: She has the choice forever, until the imam stops her and gives her the choice. This has reached me from him."
"12663","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed that Ibn Masud said: If she is freed while with a slave, and she did not know she has the choice, or she did not choose until her husband was freed, or until she dies or he dies, they inherit from one another."
"12664","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, they said: When she is freed while with a freeman, there is no choice."
"12665","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, and from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, they said: When she is freed while with a freeman, there is no choice for her. Would she choose while she is with her equal?"
"12666","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, and al-Thawri from Abd Allah from Nafi, and al-Thawri from Ubayd Allah from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When she is freed while with a freeman, there is no choice for her."
"12667","From Mamar, from Asim, from al-Shabi, he said: When she is freed while with a freeman, she has the choice."
"12668","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Shabi, he said: She is given the choice whether she was with a freeman or with a slave."
"12669","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: When she is freed while with a freeman, she has the choice."
"12670","From Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: The husband of Barirah was free."
"12671","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Aishah, that the husband of Barirah was free."
"12672","From Mamar, and Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: When she is freed while with a freeman she has the choice; if she wishes she stays with him, and if she wishes she leaves him. Ibn Jurayj said: And Hasan ibn Muslim said similar."
"12673","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: When she is freed while with a freeman, she has the choice."
"12674","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: She is given the choice, even if she is under a Qurashi."
"12675","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to a freed slave woman who had a husband: I shall mention to you a matter, and there is no blame upon you if you do not do it, but I am scrupulous about concealing it from you: You have the choice over your husband."
"12676","From Ibn Jurayj, that Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd had a slave boy and a slave girl between whom she arranged marriage, then she wanted to free the slave woman but feared she would leave her husband, so she began and freed her husband first, then freed her. Nafi said: She hated her husband, and she feared she would choose to separate from him."
"12677","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a slave woman freed while with a slave, then he was freed before she chose anything, while she was in her waiting period, he said: She has the choice."
"12678","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a slave woman freed under a slave before consummation, he said: She has the choice; if she chooses herself before consummation, she has half the dower."
"12679","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: She has nothing if she chooses herself. Mamar said: And it is the more beloved of the two sayings to me."
"12680","From Hushaym, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, concerning a man who married a slave woman for a named dower, then her masters freed her before he consummated with her, that Ibn Shubrumah said: The dower belongs to the masters."
"12681","From al-Thawri, concerning a slave woman who was with a freeman, then she was freed, he said: If he had intercourse with her while she did not know she has a choice, then they commit an offense after that, they are flogged and not stoned. If she was given the choice and chose him, then he had intercourse with her, then they commit it after that intercourse, they are stoned. If she chose him but he did not have intercourse with her until they commit it, they are flogged."
"12682","From al-Thawri, from Firas, from al-Shabi, he said: The mukatabah is given the choice."
"12683","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ata, he said: If their master contracts emancipation with both of them and frees them, she remains his wife as she is; there is no choice for her."
"12684","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: And the slave contracted emancipation for his wife and informed her, and she was freed. He said: She has more right to her affair."
"12685","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: If he helped her in her contract payment, she has no choice. And Firas said: From al-Shabi: She is given the choice, even if he helped her in her contract payment."
"12686","From al-Thawri, he said: And it is said: If he married her while she was a mukatabah, she has no choice, but if he married her before the contract, she has the choice."
"12687","From al-Thawri, he said: Our companions said: Umm al-walad is given the choice when her master dies while she has a husband, as are the mudabbara and the mukatabah; and from a freeman also, they have the choice."
"12688","From al-Thawri concerning the mukatab, that when he and his wife who is a mukatabah pay what is upon them, his wife is given the choice. [Source text garbled at opening isnad.]"
"12689","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, concerning a man who married a mukatabah, then she was freed while with him, he said: She has no choice."
"12690","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: She has no choice."
"12691","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: She has no choice."
"12692","From Mamar, from Asim, from al-Shabi, and Ayyub from Ibn Sirin, they said: She has the choice."
"12693","From Mamar, from a man, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: She has the choice, even if he helped her in her contract payment."
"12694","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying concerning the slave woman under a man: There is no harm in buying her, freeing her, then marrying her."
"12695","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: A man had a wife, then he bought her and freed her. He said: She is not a wife; he begins a new marriage and a dower, because he owned her, so ownership effaced slavery and marriage."
"12696","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a man under whom is a wife, then he bought her and freed her, he said: He marries her with a new marriage and gives her a dower, for the first marriage has ended."
"12697","From Mamar, from Qatadah, concerning a woman who married a slave, he said: When she owns anything of him she becomes unlawful for him. If she wishes she may free him and marry him, and that separation counts as a divorce."
"12698","From Mamar, from Ata ibn al-Saib, he said: I came to Madinah and said: Who of its people is most knowledgeable? They all directed me to Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah. So I came to him and said: A woman whose husband was a slave, then she bought him? He said: If she keeps him as property they are separated, but if she frees him he remains upon her marriage, with no dower and no waiting period. Mamar said, and it reached me from al-Nakhai the same. Mamar said, and Qatadah said: He separates from her, no."
"12699","From Ibn Uyaynah, he said: Urwah informed me, he said: Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq wrote to me asking me to ask about a woman whose husband was a slave, then she inherited him. So I asked Amir al-Shabi, and he said: If she frees him at that time, they remain upon their marriage, but if she keeps him as property they are separated."
"12700","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata, or he was asked, about a man who married his umm walad to his slave, then the master died leaving a child from that umm walad. He said: They are separated, because something of the slave has come to belong to her child. Her child said in the saying of Ata: When she owns anything of him she becomes unlawful for him."
"12701","From Mamar, he said: It reached me from an unnamed man: When he marries his umm walad to his slave boy, then the master dies, she has the choice; if she chooses her husband they are not separated. It was said to Mamar: But she has a son from her master, so her husband has come to belong to that son of hers? He said: The child belongs to his mother and he is a slave, so he marries the umm walad of his master. He said: And they are not separated. Al-Zuhri said: A man takes nothing from the wealth of his child except when he is in need, then he spends in a fair manner. And Mamar mentioned it from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, similar to the saying of Ata when he said: And if his son has a slave girl, he takes her and has intercourse with her. Qatadah said: What he said did not please me. [Source contains ellipsis lacuna in isnad.]"
"12702","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who married a slave woman, then bought part of her, he said: She becomes unlawful for him until he obtains her fully. If he has intercourse with her and she bears a child, she is among the ummahat al-awlad, and she is valued for his partners. Mamar said, and Qatadah said: She was not valued from him except a little, and she remains in her state."
"12703","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, that his father was asked about her, and he said: She is not his wife; she is his slave girl, as if he disliked it."
"12704","From al-Thawri, from Ashath, from al-Hakam, he said: I asked Ibrahim about a slave woman under a free man, then he inherits part of her, or a free woman whom a slave marries, then she inherits part of him. He said: When one of them inherits anything from the other, the marriage is nullified."
"12705","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, and Jabir from al-Shabi, concerning the freeman under whom is a slave woman, then he buys her, he said: No; the purchase nullifies the marriage, and she remains with him by right of ownership."
